1
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:07,810
(3. Today's the Opportunity)

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:10,180
It's the cheapest today.
Must a war start today?

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:11,610
- It's cheap today.
- It's because...

4
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:12,910
- We won't start the war.
- Tomorrow...

5
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:14,250
- We won't start the war.
- We won't start the war.

6
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:15,980
It makes sense for them to pay for war...

7
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,290
and start a war.

8
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:20,360
If we fail to make a deal,

9
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:23,220
we have to run right away
to start a war with Team Red today.

10
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,290
This is what I think.

11
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,530
That is, if we fail to make a deal.

12
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:28,300
If those two teams join forces,

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,730
we're doomed.

14
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,430
I brought it up first.

15
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:33,530
It was my idea.

16
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,000
We had to go to war.

17
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,040
If we are to go to war once now or later,

18
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,510
we must strike first.

19
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:40,380
If war breaks out,

20
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,110
it was written that
the side with more numbers...

21
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:44,280
would have an advantage.

22
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:48,150
So I thought it would be a good idea
to be on good terms with Team White.

23
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:52,520
- Hello.
- Hello.

24
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,990
- Hello.
- Hello.

25
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,790
Hi.

26
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:00,060
Hello.

27
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:04,100
For various reasons...

28
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:07,170
including the war announcement,

29
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:09,040
I thought we needed to...

30
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,710
- talk about our needs.
- Right.

31
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:13,040
We must stay alive...

32
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,140
- for our money to be meaningful.
- Right.

33
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:15,840
We must have money
for our lives to have meaning.

34
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,150
The reason for contacting you
was based on these needs.

35
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:21,480
First of all,
we're curious about your thoughts.

36
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,120
Would you want to form an alliance?

37
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,790
Or if you wish to avoid going to war,

38
00:01:25,790 --> 00:01:27,690
will you keep things peaceful?

39
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:30,160
This is our direction.

40
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,200
It will be inevitable for us
to have our members eliminated...

41
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,560
due to limited lives.

42
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:40,070
We wish to live in peace
before that moment comes.

43
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:43,570
We don't want to make sacrifices.

44
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,370
What are your thoughts?

45
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:47,210
Do you have plans
to start a war in advance?

46
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:49,210
This is something
we have different opinions on.

47
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:50,680
- You have different opinions?
- We have different opinions.

48
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,910
(War)

49
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:56,250
(Peace)

50
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,090
(War)

51
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:02,320
What do you think is the advantage...

52
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:04,190
of starting a war in advance?

53
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:06,090
The fee for going to war...

54
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:07,830
- It can get more expensive?
- can get more expensive.

55
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:09,260
A loss was inevitable,

56
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:11,030
and that was based on the current price.

57
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:13,570
Whether that will get reduced
or increased over time,

58
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:16,200
I believe that wasn't...

59
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,270
explained to us in detail.

60
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:20,040
For us to reduce the damage
all of us might go through...

61
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,010
and to leave this place
with the biggest amount of money,

62
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:25,250
starting a war quickly
might be the answer.

63
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:27,450
We will lose people anyway...

64
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:29,880
- and if that's from the opposing team,
- Right.

65
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:31,790
you wish to secure...

66
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:33,750
- a greater amount of prize money, right?
- Right.

67
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,920
Everyone will suffer
the least damage at this point.

68
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,090
The fee for going to war...

69
00:02:38,090 --> 00:02:39,890
- will get revealed first.
- Right.

70
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:42,160
The value of the diamonds at that point...

71
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,930
gets decided by us.

72
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,970
The rule states that it's based on
the value of diamonds...

73
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:48,900
- when the fee is paid.
- Right.

74
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,870
- So even if the fee...
- It's based on the number of diamonds.

75
00:02:50,870 --> 00:02:52,470
becomes 30 diamonds from 15 diamonds,

76
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:54,510
- We can change the value.
- we can change...

77
00:02:54,510 --> 00:02:56,780
the actual value in reality.

78
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:58,250
Before war breaks out,

79
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,380
we can change the value of the currency.

80
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:04,390
- We can lower the price like that.
- I see.

81
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:07,390
If we are to join forces,

82
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:10,320
- we can minimize our loss.
- Right.

83
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:12,660
We have that ability.

84
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:17,430
If we decide to work together,
we will be 9 against 3.

85
00:03:17,930 --> 00:03:19,770
- We'll be greater in number.
- That's a big advantage.

86
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:21,740
- That's a big advantage.
- Right.

87
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,170
Actually, later on,

88
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:28,280
we will produce a lot more,

89
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,580
and if we have more things
in our possession,

90
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,250
- the value of half becomes much bigger.
- It becomes much bigger.

91
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:33,750
We believe a greater war will come...

92
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,680
if we decide to hold off on going to war.

93
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,120
If we are going to go to war anyway,

94
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,760
I thought it might be better for us
to secure peace instead.

95
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:43,390
But let's say we do go to war early.

96
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:46,230
There's no guarantee
that a second war will not break out.

97
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:48,400
Right. Let's say a war breaks out.

98
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,270
Our war deterrent
is issuing more diamonds.

99
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:53,000
If we do that a lot,

100
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,800
war will break out again.

101
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,940
- It will happen again and again.
- Right.

102
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:57,570
Why sit around
when the currency is so low?

103
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,740
It will become,
"Let's go to war to kill time."

104
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,140
The losing side...

105
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,640
- will have no more to lose.
- Right.

106
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:03,680
- They will start another war.
- Right.

107
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,910
- That will be their only option.
- Right.

108
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:05,950
It will become, "One of us will die."

109
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:07,550
As if it's an arms race,

110
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:09,050
teams will continue to
pay the fee for war.

111
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:11,150
- That will keep reducing the prize money.
- Right.

112
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:12,590
Once a war breaks out,

113
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:14,990
everyone will suffer a loss.

114
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,930
There's no big reason
to start a war at this point.

115
00:04:17,930 --> 00:04:19,330
- We still have time to...
- Then,

116
00:04:19,330 --> 00:04:22,430
I think it's right for us
make at least a verbal contract.

117
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,560
- Why don't we write a contract?
- We should do that.

118
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:26,370
If we decide to join forces with Team Red,

119
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:27,900
it will be inevitable...

120
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:30,270
for both sides to suffer harm.

121
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:33,640
If it becomes 6 on 6, it will become
a bloody war for both sides.

122
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:40,950
What we can offer first...

123
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,580
- is a priority for trading with us.
- Right.

124
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:45,520
You can become the first ones...

125
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:46,920
- To negotiate with you?
- to negotiate with us.

126
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,990
- Before Team Red.
- Right.

127
00:04:49,090 --> 00:04:50,120
- That's great.
- That's great.

128
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,130
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

129
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:54,130
The priority for negotiating for lives...

130
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:55,360
will be great for us.

131
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:59,270
Issuing diamonds
will be inevitable for us.

132
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,140
We are still able to adjust the rate.

133
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:05,110
We believe we have no reason
to make diamonds worth close to nothing.

134
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,940
We can tell you that...

135
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:10,080
we will maintain the value of diamonds.

136
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,310
If we consider ourselves as one team,

137
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:15,220
until it is inevitable for us...

138
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,490
to eat our own members alive,

139
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,590
we will consider that our opponents
are outside of us.

140
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:26,760
The leaders should shake hands.

141
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,930
- We should shake hands.
- We should shake hands.

142
00:05:28,930 --> 00:05:31,130
- I'm sorry for having sweaty hands.
- This is quite sudden.

143
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,470
I wish us the best.

144
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:34,040
- The Town Hall Treaty.
- The Town Hall Treaty.

145
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:36,040
- The Town Hall Treaty.
- The Town Hall Treaty.

146
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,710
The Town Hall Non-Aggression Treaty.

147
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:41,440
Fortunately,
Team White was friendly with us.

148
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,680
The six of them looked solid,

149
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:45,980
and that was why we wanted to
join forces with them.

150
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,520
But on second thought,

151
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,280
I belatedly thought that...

152
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:52,390
everything was designed
for us to be needed by them.

153
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,620
A 2-on-1 alliance was formed.

154
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:58,030
"Should we kill off Team Red
except for one last member?"

155
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,590
This suggestion could have been made...

156
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:02,200
if we were to be cruel.

157
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,930
But if that happens,
our team will have a greater influence...

158
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:06,400
in the long term.

159
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,040
Well, 3 plus 1 will still only be 4.

160
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,010
After a war breaks out,

161
00:06:11,010 --> 00:06:13,970
the teams in that alliance
will go to war again.

162
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:16,940
I believe it will become
White against Blue.

163
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:18,480
But we are greater in number.

164
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,050
That means we have the advantage.

165
00:06:20,050 --> 00:06:22,580
I was surprised that
they wanted to join forces with us first.

166
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:25,420
It will be great for us
if they didn't think that far.

167
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,820
There's no such thing as trust here.

168
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,860
But I do want to make them trust me.

169
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:32,290
I hate the commission so much.

170
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:35,060
It's unreasonable for us.

171
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:37,730
They keep pushing us
to pay the commission,

172
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,530
- Right.
- and I can't stand it.

173
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:41,540
They should pay!

174
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:44,840
For every deal we've made,

175
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:47,270
we've paid the commission.

176
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:49,510
Well, it makes sense
to a certain extent...

177
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:51,650
as we're the ones
who are collecting the credits.

178
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:54,010
But if this keeps happening,

179
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:57,420
we have to pay the commission
for every deal we make.

180
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:00,390
They don't seem to know
how generous we are.

181
00:07:00,490 --> 00:07:01,660
They will never think that way.

182
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,320
This is what Team Blue will be thinking.

183
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,160
"We're sharing life."

184
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:08,060
Hold on. I see stairs over there.

185
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,130
Is this Black's house?

186
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:10,830
(They spot Black's dormitory
that is secluded.)

187
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:12,500
Won't it be fine if we stay outside?

188
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,530
Right.

189
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:17,300
There was something I was obsessed with
after coming here.

190
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:19,140
It's the passcode on the wall.

191
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,540
Based on my deduction,

192
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,810
there seemed to be 1 code
in each of the 4 houses...

193
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:25,280
as there were four boxes.

194
00:07:25,410 --> 00:07:27,310
I wanted to collect those codes.

195
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:30,420
(Rummaging)

196
00:07:33,050 --> 00:07:34,890
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

197
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:35,960
Hello.

198
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,630
We're here
to take a look at Black's house.

199
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:38,730
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

200
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,460
There must be nothing here.

201
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:41,530
There's nothing here.

202
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,000
Well,

203
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,700
if there was a way to barge inside,

204
00:07:46,870 --> 00:07:49,800
I would've gone in even if it cost me
all of my diamonds.

205
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,310
But there's a rule that we can't
enter someone else's dorm.

206
00:07:52,470 --> 00:07:54,440
Maillard seems to be...

207
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,910
suspicious of everything.

208
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:57,380
It felt so scary.

209
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:00,080
- Gosh, Black's house.
- Black was home.

210
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:01,750
(Laughing)

211
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:07,050
You haven't answered any of
the skill development questions, right?

212
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:08,190
Oh, I still haven't answered any of them.

213
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:09,590
I was a madman.

214
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,720
Really?

215
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:13,090
Even when I went down earlier,

216
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:14,830
he seemed to be answering several of them.

217
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:16,330
I'd like to make a suggestion.

218
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,730
If I reveal the questions
of the other teams,

219
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,100
that will cause harm to them.

220
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,840
If we get the right answer?

221
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:25,570
I could instead offer...

222
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:26,970
not to answer Team Red's questions.

223
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:29,580
Having a skill...

224
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:33,550
could be a great advantage
at the negotiating table.

225
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,320
- This is what I think.
- Right.

226
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:38,190
I kept approaching them
with a stance of...

227
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:39,820
wanting to be Team Red's cooperator.

228
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,890
I tried my best to listen
to Maillard's words.

229
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,460
I solved questions with him...

230
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,430
and tried to win his favor.

231
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:50,000
We came here first...

232
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,100
after deciding on our priority.

233
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:54,400
We can't offer you a lot
as we don't have much.

234
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,040
I was wondering if you have
earned yourself a lot today.

235
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:59,810
Did you earn lives?

236
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,340
Well, what can I reveal?

237
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,150
- We are planning to reveal everything...
- As for us...

238
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:08,150
- about us.
- Really? Well, it's quite obvious.

239
00:09:08,150 --> 00:09:09,550
- Right.
- It's obvious.

240
00:09:09,650 --> 00:09:11,550
We made a deal for lives.

241
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:13,650
- The efficiency...
- It's different.

242
00:09:13,650 --> 00:09:15,620
- I believe it will be very different.
- Right.

243
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,060
That is why we think...

244
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,960
you have earned a lot.

245
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:20,900
- It was quite hard.
- Harder than you thought?

246
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,900
The questions were quite hard for us.

247
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,100
We expected to earn a lot.

248
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:27,030
Anyway, we weren't able to
earn a lot today.

249
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:28,970
So you don't have many lives
to offer to us.

250
00:09:28,970 --> 00:09:30,440
We don't have a lot...

251
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,740
- that can be traded off.
- You don't have a lot?

252
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,670
- How many are they in number?
- Actually...

253
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:36,180
The number of lives
we were willing to trade off...

254
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:37,550
- was two.
- Two.

255
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:39,050
- Oh, really?
- Well,

256
00:09:39,050 --> 00:09:41,580
we thought you would've been able
to earn 3 or 4.

257
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,050
- No.
- That is impossible.

258
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:44,520
- It's impossible with our efficiency.
- Our efficiency is low.

259
00:09:44,590 --> 00:09:45,590
- It's really bad for us.
- Ten questions were answered.

260
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:47,450
- But...
- You must've earned around two.

261
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,360
(Team White's actual output, 2 lives)

262
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:55,400
So all we can do...

263
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,460
is purchase however many you offer.

264
00:09:57,830 --> 00:10:00,330
So, for today,

265
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:03,470
if we offer you two or more,
that will mean...

266
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:05,240
we will be losing one of ours.

267
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,980
But that will keep all six of you alive.

268
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,740
- Right.
- If we offer you two,

269
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:12,510
you will need two more tomorrow.

270
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:14,480
- We will produce more tomorrow.
- Right.

271
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:17,280
We will offer you two more
after earning them tomorrow.

272
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,650
If we fail to earn our lives,

273
00:10:19,650 --> 00:10:21,360
- we will offer up what we have.
- Right.

274
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,660
- That sounds good.
- Tomorrow,

275
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,460
- we will secure two lives for you.
- We'll do that.

276
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,530
Sounds good.

277
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:26,890
- How much is each life?
- The price.

278
00:10:26,890 --> 00:10:28,630
We didn't talk about the price of them.

279
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,830
- Yesterday, one life...
- Ten diamonds.

280
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:32,570
was worth 10 diamonds,
which is 10,000 dollars.

281
00:10:32,570 --> 00:10:34,400
We'll be honest.

282
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,440
We didn't issue more diamonds.

283
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,840
- Right.
- The prices are the same now.

284
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:40,740
But after our deal yesterday,

285
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,710
I noticed that the other teams...

286
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,810
have a lot more of the prize money
split among the members.

287
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,280
They have the most.

288
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,150
(The members of Team White
have 14 diamonds each.)

289
00:10:48,650 --> 00:10:52,890
You must've traded off around 50
to Team Red yesterday.

290
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,160
The prize money value for each of us...

291
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,690
is quite low,

292
00:10:58,690 --> 00:11:00,560
so we decided to offer
half of what we offered yesterday.

293
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:03,930
If we plan to issue a lot of diamonds,

294
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:05,530
we can offer to trade off a lot.

295
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,070
- Well...
- We'll take some time...

296
00:11:07,070 --> 00:11:08,740
- to discuss the price.
- Right.

297
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,670
Team White will be able to survive
until tomorrow...

298
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:12,970
even without our lives.

299
00:11:12,970 --> 00:11:14,380
If we refuse to give them
our lives the next day,

300
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:18,110
war will break out inevitably.

301
00:11:18,310 --> 00:11:21,050
To prevent war,

302
00:11:21,050 --> 00:11:23,720
we must offer them our lives.

303
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:27,150
What's worth 1 day for them
will be worth 2 days for us.

304
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:29,090
That puts a lot more pressure on us.

305
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:33,790
But we need to get a bit more.

306
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,260
If we get two,

307
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,970
there's a big chance
someone will get eliminated from our team.

308
00:11:37,970 --> 00:11:40,530
You saw them calculate
the exact number, right?

309
00:11:40,530 --> 00:11:41,700
She said, "If we trade off two,"

310
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,170
"you will need two more tomorrow."

311
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:47,070
(Current lives of Team White: 8)

312
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:50,080
(Genie predicted the exact number.)

313
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,650
But if we get two,

314
00:11:51,650 --> 00:11:53,450
we can all live today and tomorrow.

315
00:11:53,450 --> 00:11:55,450
Are we going to secure
just enough to survive each day?

316
00:11:55,550 --> 00:11:57,350
Without a single life saved up?

317
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,350
A person will make a sudden change
if there's no backup.

318
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:02,390
- Team Red might charge at us.
- Half price or...

319
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:03,920
- Ten?
- Fifteen?

320
00:12:04,490 --> 00:12:06,290
We don't want to trigger them...

321
00:12:06,290 --> 00:12:08,830
- when they're short on lives.
- Should we ask for 12?

322
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:10,530
- We should ask for 12.
- Right.

323
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:11,970
We made the decision quickly.

324
00:12:11,970 --> 00:12:14,200
- We'll ask for 12.
- You'll ask for 12?

325
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,140
We were talking,

326
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:18,010
and it felt like we were dayflies.

327
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:20,840
Getting two lives now...

328
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,640
and securing two for tomorrow
is very different.

329
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,980
Through the productive activities,

330
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:27,180
you might not be able to earn a lot...

331
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:28,850
because the questions are too hard.

332
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:32,090
If that happens,
we might not be able to secure six lives.

333
00:12:32,090 --> 00:12:33,250
We will feel a lot more relieved

334
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:34,390
- with just one more.
- That's right.

335
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:36,290
What we're asking for is for your team...

336
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:38,530
to trade off your future lives...

337
00:12:38,530 --> 00:12:40,530
to secure our near future.

338
00:12:40,530 --> 00:12:42,930
- I believe that will feel like a risk.
- This is our plea.

339
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:46,630
Are you willing to hold a meeting...

340
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:50,700
to discuss offering us
more than two lives?

341
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,370
- We'll move out again.
- Right.

342
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:54,580
- Here we go.
- Right.

343
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:57,040
We'll have 4 left after spending 6 today.

344
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,680
- They will be able to drag us around.
- Right.

345
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,080
- Twelve is enough for today and tomorrow.
- That will make them...

346
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,420
- take control of our lives.
- We'll be dead after that.

347
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,820
We'll all die if they betray us.

348
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,850
If we produce two tomorrow,

349
00:13:06,850 --> 00:13:08,720
- we need four more.
- Right.

350
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,260
But will they...

351
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,030
be able to earn four
by answering the questions?

352
00:13:13,030 --> 00:13:14,660
- Right.
- They're a lot more lacking...

353
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:16,560
than we think.

354
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:20,370
I don't think offering them three
isn't a bad idea at this moment.

355
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:23,140
Should we ask for 20 diamonds
for 3 lives, then?

356
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,670
Will that be possible?

357
00:13:24,770 --> 00:13:25,910
Ask for 20 diamonds for 3 lives?

358
00:13:26,010 --> 00:13:28,340
- That's asking for one more.
- Right.

359
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:30,280
- We'll ask for 18 without changing it?
- Right.

360
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,350
- First of all...
- Four?

361
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,750
- I'm sorry.
- But...

362
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,380
you'll be able to produce
at least one tomorrow.

363
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,580
At least one tomorrow.

364
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:38,750
- That's not true!
- That's not what it's like.

365
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:40,020
- It isn't certain for us.
- It's really tough for us.

366
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:42,460
- But 4 from us would be...
- But 4 from us...

367
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:44,090
- Is that too tough for you?
- To be honest,

368
00:13:44,090 --> 00:13:46,860
that's nearly how many we earned today.

369
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:48,300
- I see.
- So...

370
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,460
You did really well.

371
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:52,770
(Team Blue's actual output, 5 lives)

372
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,170
We were willing to offer half of that.

373
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:58,140
As we want to be on the same track,

374
00:13:58,140 --> 00:14:02,080
- we decided to offer three lives.
- Right. That sounds good.

375
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:03,680
- We'll proceed with that deal.
- Right.

376
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,350
- But it'll be 18 diamonds for 3 lives.
- It'll be 18 diamonds...

377
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:07,780
- for 3 lives.
- It'll be 18 diamonds?

378
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,050
- One will cost six diamonds.
- Sounds good.

379
00:14:09,050 --> 00:14:10,250
- We'll go with that.
- Right.

380
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,420
That's a straightforward deal. Thank you.

381
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,490
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

382
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:15,390
We didn't have many diamonds left.

383
00:14:15,390 --> 00:14:16,890
If we went with the same deal
we made yesterday,

384
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:18,630
