a lot more diamonds,

385
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:20,560
and that would greatly lower
the value of the diamonds.

386
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,900
We did well to persuade them with this.

387
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:24,670
We didn't get a lot from them.

388
00:14:24,770 --> 00:14:28,300
But we earned their trust
because of their fear.

389
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:30,200
We weren't the ones who gave them fear.

390
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,770
They came to us out of fear.

391
00:14:31,770 --> 00:14:33,310
We didn't even threaten them.

392
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:35,810
Even though they had the upper hand,

393
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:37,710
they came to us in a lower stance.

394
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:40,780
We earned a lot more from them mentally.

395
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:43,480
After earning five,

396
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:45,390
we only wanted to offer two...

397
00:14:45,390 --> 00:14:48,390
excluding three of our lives.

398
00:14:48,390 --> 00:14:52,930
Two didn't seem like a lot
even in our eyes.

399
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:54,560
Since they needed a lot of lives,

400
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,100
they might've said,
"Please give them to us."

401
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,030
"We'll give you a lot of our diamonds."

402
00:14:58,030 --> 00:15:00,330
They might've begged us for them.

403
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:02,770
I tried to avoid those situations
as much as possible.

404
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:04,710
Three lives seemed okay to offer.

405
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:09,840
We agree with what you said.

406
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,140
We like solving questions.

407
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:12,180
Right.

408
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:15,580
- Should we move over there?
- Sure. Shall we?

409
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:19,220
You received
the skill development questions, right?

410
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,220
- Yes.
- We haven't solved them yet.

411
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:21,620
- We also haven't solved them.
- We haven't solved them yet.

412
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:23,560
- I think that team got it right.
- It's a bit...

413
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:24,760
Are the questions endless?

414
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,290
They said they got it wrong.

415
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:27,660
- Right.
- Right.

416
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:29,060
They're still together.

417
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:30,760
They were together for a long time.

418
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,300
- There's something between them.
- Red and Black.

419
00:15:32,530 --> 00:15:33,970
We're gathered together.

420
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:36,270
I'm sure this team is
wanted by them the most.

421
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,470
They might be waiting...

422
00:15:38,470 --> 00:15:40,610
- to talk.
- Should we make them feel anxious?

423
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,580
- Thank you.
- Here they are.

424
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:44,780
Nice.

425
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,650
- There's one more.
- Two.

426
00:15:47,650 --> 00:15:48,780
(All skill development questions
get revealed.)

427
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,920
- They're all the same.
- Yes.

428
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:53,320
We're just asking what you think.

429
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:55,160
The skill development questions.

430
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,060
The questions can be shared
between us, right?

431
00:15:57,060 --> 00:15:58,590
- The questions can be shared.
- What do you think?

432
00:15:58,590 --> 00:15:59,730
Since we have different answers?

433
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:00,730
- Right.
- Right.

434
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:02,430
We won't reveal each of our benefits
to each other.

435
00:16:02,430 --> 00:16:05,070
I think it'll be okay
to share the questions with each other.

436
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:06,530
Black will answer them first
if we don't get them.

437
00:16:06,530 --> 00:16:08,140
- We have to pay him.
- Exactly.

438
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:12,010
The books that we have
seem to be different.

439
00:16:12,010 --> 00:16:13,010
- We have six heads.
- Then...

440
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:14,570
- Right.
- Right.

441
00:16:14,570 --> 00:16:16,210
Do you remember the parts?

442
00:16:16,210 --> 00:16:18,380
This was what it was for the key.

443
00:16:18,550 --> 00:16:23,280
"That Monday, the tower built by greed
collapsed silently."

444
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:26,720
"From now on, if our country's culture
and economy..."

445
00:16:26,990 --> 00:16:30,460
"goes beyond rapid growth
and reaches relaxation growth..."

446
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:33,390
This seems to be Black Monday
or the Oil Shock.

447
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:34,760
Right.

448
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,300
- This is...
- Right.

449
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,470
- certainly the IMF crisis.
- Right.

450
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:41,300
I looked for answers in the books,

451
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,270
but it was too hard to guess. So this...

452
00:16:43,270 --> 00:16:44,540
The answers might be
in each other's books.

453
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:46,270
- Right. We have different books.
- Right.

454
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:49,110
(Team Blue's books)

455
00:16:49,110 --> 00:16:50,310
(Team Red's books)

456
00:16:50,310 --> 00:16:52,350
Did you have a book called "Money"
in your dorm?

457
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:55,520
- I didn't check the books at all.
- Right.

458
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:56,920
I'll look through them.

459
00:16:56,920 --> 00:17:00,550
For example, if we all have the same book,

460
00:17:00,650 --> 00:17:03,160
I feel like the hint is in that book.

461
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,160
(The hint for the question
is hidden in the books?)

462
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,130
Could it be about finding the dates?

463
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:11,000
One hour into the trading session.

464
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,530
- Could it be written?
- They're having a long conversation.

465
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:14,700
- One hour went by.
- Right.

466
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,400
I'm not sure how we're supposed
to answer them.

467
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,540
Right. That's the problem.

468
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:19,810
This is what it says
if we answer the question.

469
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:21,410
We'll just share this with you.

470
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:24,680
It says it will be applied if we answer
the skill development question.

471
00:17:24,950 --> 00:17:26,250
I wonder what this means.

472
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:28,250
"When the answer submitted is correct,"

473
00:17:28,450 --> 00:17:29,920
"the skill development..."

474
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:32,650
"and the answer
will get applied right away."

475
00:17:33,250 --> 00:17:36,190
What can be applied from this?

476
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,360
"Applied?"

477
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:40,530
It feels like something
that will actually bring a change.

478
00:17:40,530 --> 00:17:42,360
- It sounds off.
- If it's...

479
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,160
something that will get applied,

480
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,870
I understood it to be something...

481
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:47,230
that will get applied to this community.

482
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:49,400
- It's an answer...
- Right.

483
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,940
- that can be applied to this community.
- That's what it is.

484
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,340
That's a huge hint. Thank you.

485
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:57,180
- Right.
- But it's so hard to figure out.

486
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,080
We didn't read the questions in detail.

487
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:04,080
It wasn't just about getting the right
to use a certain skill.

488
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:07,420
The answer will be applied to our world
as well.

489
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,260
These were the two key points.

490
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:11,260
It's not just a skill that gets developed.

491
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:14,290
Could it be a systematic word...

492
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:16,730
that can be applied to our community?

493
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:20,000
This might turn out to be
a significant part,

494
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:23,270
so I didn't want to share about it
with another team.

495
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:24,970
Salt went,

496
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:27,040
"There was this as well."

497
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:29,440
She shared everything I said.

498
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:32,050
(Genie)

499
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:33,410
"All right, then."

500
00:18:34,710 --> 00:18:38,490
- Well...
- They all seem to be related.

501
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,320
It would be great to hear from Team Red.

502
00:18:40,390 --> 00:18:41,490
Should we split up, then?

503
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:43,390
We'll talk to Black.

504
00:18:43,390 --> 00:18:44,690
- Sounds good.
- Sounds good.

505
00:18:44,690 --> 00:18:45,960
- What about our deal?
- Then...

506
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,190
- We must make our deal.
- We must do that now.

507
00:18:47,190 --> 00:18:48,300
We'll make our deal first.

508
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:49,700
- Our leaders should move.
- We'll meet there.

509
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,500
- Let's meet again at night.
- Right.

510
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,100
They've agreed to make a deal.

511
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,070
You've agreed to make a deal.

512
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,510
- Yes. We'll complete our deal.
- Right.

513
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,540
Leader.

514
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:03,410
Should we wait to talk to Team Red?

515
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,750
Three of us should stay here.

516
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:07,750
Wait if they contact us first.

517
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:09,680
- And wait for...
- Get going first.

518
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,750
Okay.

519
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:12,920
What's something that occurs...

520
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,320
as soon as a skill is developed?

521
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:18,260
What would be interesting
if it were to get applied right now?

522
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,430
That's a good approach.

523
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,630
Gosh.

524
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:26,800
(Salt heads over to get the resources
as Team Blue's leader.)

525
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:29,770
What was it again?

526
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:32,340
"Market's Memory," "Fifty Things
That Made the Modern Economy,"

527
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,640
"What Did Scientists Do in the War?"

528
00:19:35,410 --> 00:19:36,980
The word "war..."

529
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,850
is really scary.

530
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,680
I don't have to take all of them with me.

531
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:44,150
Without going to war,

532
00:19:44,890 --> 00:19:47,120
I hope we can live in peace
with each other.

533
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:51,190
To be honest, there's a big chance
for Team White to have...

534
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,960
- the first one to get eliminated.
- We expected it to be us.

535
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,000
- Everyone would think that.
- Right.

536
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,930
That could happen.

537
00:19:56,930 --> 00:19:58,400
Gosh. This is a big workout.

538
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,630
- It's exhausting, right?
- It's a big workout.

539
00:19:59,630 --> 00:20:01,000
- We'll be back.
- We'll wait here.

540
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
We'll be back.

541
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,070
Gosh!

542
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:08,580
These can't go to waste.

543
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,140
- Oh, no!
- Hold on.

544
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:12,480
- Hold on!
- Hold on.

545
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,250
That's how it'll be.

546
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:15,380
Gosh, it got spilled.

547
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,580
What a mess.

548
00:20:18,650 --> 00:20:19,720
Thank you.

549
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,560
I became someone who threw out
money on the floor.

550
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:23,920
- This is worth so much.
- Gosh!

551
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:26,660
You look very rich. How nice.

552
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:28,360
I'm sure you won't,

553
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:31,570
but you might get worried
that I might steal it.

554
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,900
Thank you.

555
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:35,270
(Team White pays the one credit.)

556
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:39,940
You must go that way.

557
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:42,140
Right.

558
00:20:42,510 --> 00:20:43,680
Why did you leave it there?

559
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,850
- This is Team White's side. I'm sorry.
- Right.

560
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:47,480
I must be stupid.

561
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,620
Out of the ones we have...

562
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:53,690
(Trade: 3 lives for 18 diamonds)

563
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:56,790
Must I show you like this?

564
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:58,960
No. There will be a check
once you submit them.

565
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,490
There will be a check?

566
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:04,560
- You must get it checked first.
- We're checking the submitted amount.

567
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:06,770
Please wait a moment.

568
00:21:07,170 --> 00:21:09,670
A leader with experience feels different.

569
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,540
The trade has been completed.

570
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:14,070
Thank you.

571
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:19,250
It's hard to move back and forth...

572
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:20,410
as we're at the top.

573
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:21,720
But actually...

574
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:23,720
Will you not buy credits today?

575
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:25,250
We can't make decisions.

576
00:21:25,250 --> 00:21:26,990
- We'll move over when she returns.
- We'll move with our leader.

577
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:28,760
Can't we just start talking now?

578
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:31,860
We have to talk to two teams.

579
00:21:31,890 --> 00:21:33,990
- Please give us a moment.
- She went to make a trade.

580
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:39,030
I was surprised by
Team White's change of attitude.

581
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:41,130
They didn't seem to be in need of credits.

582
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:44,640
A trade with Team White
isn't necessary today.

583
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:48,310
There's an awareness that things are...

584
00:21:48,410 --> 00:21:49,740
getting tougher for us.

585
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:51,510
The value of credits...

586
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,980
is only found in productive activities.

587
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:58,080
They can only be used for hints
and retries.

588
00:21:58,080 --> 00:22:00,320
If we start saving up on them,

589
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:04,160
just two credits might be needed
for a trade for lives...

590
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:06,760
along with question answering.

591
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,800
Things have become quite awkward for us.

592
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:13,070
I don't want to give it to Black
all of a sudden.

593
00:22:13,470 --> 00:22:15,700
- No.
- No. We can't be like that.

594
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:17,200
We can't be naive...

595
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:18,870
and trust only Team White.

596
00:22:18,870 --> 00:22:20,170
- You're right about that.
- Right.

597
00:22:20,170 --> 00:22:23,380
We'll talk to Black
as we've made a promise.

598
00:22:24,210 --> 00:22:26,880
(Vector asked for a life in the morning.)

599
00:22:27,050 --> 00:22:28,450
But we can't trade with each other.

600
00:22:28,450 --> 00:22:31,050
I'll make a black market.

601
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,220
That's possible?

602
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:33,390
I don't know.

603
00:22:33,390 --> 00:22:34,490
I'm going to give it a try.

604
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:37,690
This is my offer.

605
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:39,730
If you give me a life,

606
00:22:39,730 --> 00:22:42,260
I'll provide you with the food you want
for two days.

607
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,730
Let's take everything now.

608
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,600
We must not get caught.

609
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:48,130
(Team Blue got food
for giving him a life.)

610
00:22:48,130 --> 00:22:49,840
I wanted to wear something big
for a reason.

611
00:22:50,370 --> 00:22:52,670
- You must give me a life.
- Of course.

612
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,970
If he opens the supermarket tomorrow,

613
00:22:54,970 --> 00:22:57,410
everyone will know that
we gave him a life.

614
00:22:57,410 --> 00:23:00,480
We should come up with an excuse.

615
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:03,680
How should we put it?

616
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:05,050
Actually,

617
00:23:05,150 --> 00:23:06,450
all we did was...

618
00:23:06,450 --> 00:23:08,360
to give him a life for food.

619
00:23:08,590 --> 00:23:09,820
That's true,

620
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:11,590
but talking to Black...

621
00:23:11,590 --> 00:23:14,360
after talking to Team White...

622
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,830
could be something
that could break their trust.

623
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,730
- That is what concerns me.
- Right.

624
00:23:19,030 --> 00:23:20,330
Right.

625
00:23:20,330 --> 00:23:23,500
We gave away a life after saying
we were short on lives.

626
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,040
Could we have a moment, Black?

627
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:28,440
(Team Blue asks for
a sudden meeting with Black.)

628
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:33,580
You are in need...

629
00:23:33,580 --> 00:23:35,550
- of lives as well.
- Right.

630
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:37,580
It's a matter of life and death for them.

631
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:40,550
They're all complaining about
wanting more lives.

632
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,790
We're going,

633
00:23:41,790 --> 00:23:44,320
"This is all we can give you."

634
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:47,630
But it's quite awkward to say,
"We got some food from Black..."

635
00:23:47,630 --> 00:23:48,830
"and gave him a life."

636
00:23:48,830 --> 00:23:50,660
- I don't know what to say.
- Well,

637
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:52,370
we're not saying
we're not going to give you a life.

638
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:53,830
- We'll give you a life,
- Right.

639
00:23:53,830 --> 00:23:54,970
but when we do,

640
00:23:54,970 --> 00:23:56,340
- There should be a cause.
- there should be a cause.

641
00:23:56,340 --> 00:23:58,200
We're asking what we can do about this.

642
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,640
How does this sound?

643
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:02,380
"We made a promise that Black will not..."

644
00:24:02,380 --> 00:24:04,410
"work on our skill development question."

645
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:07,550
After securing our safety,

646
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:10,780
we can say that Black
took that into consideration.

647
00:24:10,780 --> 00:24:12,220
That might work.

648
00:24:12,220 --> 00:24:13,820
She's a genius today.

649
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:16,120
But you have to...

650
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:17,560
- take part in this with us.
- That's right.

651
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:20,330
- Then,
- I think that's a good idea.

652
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:22,360
- I'll think it through before dinner.
- Right.

653
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:24,460
I'll see if it's a reasonable idea.

654
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:25,830
We'll meet after that.

655
00:24:25,830 --> 00:24:27,270
- Right.
- Thank you.

656
00:24:27,630 --> 00:24:29,370
I can survive for another day.

657
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,810
Could we have a conversation?

658
00:24:31,810 --> 00:24:33,410
Should we? Sounds good.

659
00:24:33,410 --> 00:24:35,640
- Are you busy?
- Gosh.

660
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,010
We have a lot of things to carry.

661
00:24:37,010 --> 00:24:39,180
- Could we put back our things?
- Sure.

662
00:24:39,180 --> 00:24:40,980
There's not much time left until dinner.

663
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:42,750
- I'll be quick.
- Okay.

664
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:43,880
See you later.

665
00:24:45,020 --> 00:24:46,750
What can we talk about with Team Red?

666
00:24:47,290 --> 00:24:49,590
It won't hurt to talk.

667
00:24:49,590 --> 00:24:50,820
I did tell them...

668
00:24:50,820 --> 00:24:52,530
we had to visit the dorm
to come up with a plan.

669
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:55,460
When we first talked to Team Blue,

670
00:24:55,460 --> 00:24:57,060
they said they had too many things...

671
00:24:57,060 --> 00:24:58,870
and will be back from their dorm.

672
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:00,500
That was when I realized...

673
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:03,740
they didn't want to sell their lives.

674
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:05,640
"What must we do for our lives?"

675
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:08,310
"Must we produce lives tomorrow?"

676
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,410
These talks began between us.

677
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:13,850
If we are to make things ideal for us,

678
00:25:13,850 --> 00:25:16,080
we have to contact Team Red
when Team Blue is not around.

679
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:17,550
- We have to contact Team Red.
- Right.

680
00:25:17,550 --> 00:25:19,320
This is our advantage
with our greater number.

681
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:21,790
If they are to start a war,

682
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:24,020
we can go, "Form an alliance with us."

683
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:26,030
The moment we betray them,

684
00:25:26,030 --> 00:25:27,060
we can take the win.

685
00:25:27,060 --> 00:25:28,390
We can earn their lives like that.

686
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:29,900
It's the same for us,

687
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,730
whether we win with one or the other.

688
00:25:31,830 --> 00:25:33,770
It will be the same 6-on-3 fight...

689
00:25:33,770 --> 00:25:35,340
after we win with any team.

690
00:25:35,340 --> 00:25:36,570
The best thing...

691
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,270
is to persuade Team Blue or Team Red...

692
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:40,640
with, "We will help you
if you start a war."

693
00:25:40,870 --> 00:25:43,140
- Right.
- That becomes a huge win for us.

694
00:25:43,380 --> 00:25:45,710
"Even if you form an alliance
with the other team,"

695
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:47,310
"you will get destroyed in a war."

696
00:25:47,310 --> 00:25:49,220
If the other two teams form an alliance,

697
00:25:49,380 --> 00:25:52,420
we can issue a lot of diamonds...

698
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:54,090
and make a lot of weapons.

699
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:56,390
We can destroy them after that.

700
00:25:56,390 --> 00:25:58,260
We can't trust Team White.

701
00:25:58,260 --> 00:26:01,460
They sat with Team Red
for another conversation.

702
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:06,830
(They spotted Team Red and Team White
having a conversation.)

703
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:08,670
- What's funny is this.
- Right.

704
00:26:08,670 --> 00:26:10,500
Blue wasn't able to produce
a lot of lives.

705
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:11,740
They only produced two.

706
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:12,870
- Really?
- Yes.

707
00:26:12,870 --> 00:26:13,970
- Team Blue?
- Yes.

708
00:26:13,970 --> 00:26:15,010
(Vector lies about their life output.)

709
00:26:15,010 --> 00:26:17,410
We'll be able to produce more than them.

710
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:19,210
- We should produce lives tomorrow.
- Right.

711
00:26:19,210 --> 00:26:20,210
Tell Team Blue...

712
00:26:20,210 --> 00:26:21,650
- to stay out of our sight.
- Right. Shall we go for it?

713
00:26:21,650 --> 00:26:23,950
Team Red will produce lives now!

714
00:26:24,150 --> 00:26:26,450
We might be able to sell lives
if we do a good job.

715
00:26:26,450 --> 00:26:27,450
Right.

716
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:29,190
- We should just...
- When you talk with them,

717
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:30,820
don't be like, "You only produced two."

718
00:26:30,820 --> 00:26:32,830
- Don't point that out to them.
- Never.

719
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:34,630
- Never.
- I have to get lives...

720
00:26:34,630 --> 00:26:36,800
- from Team Blue as well.
- Understood.

721
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:39,430
Vector kept saying these phrases
starting from yesterday.

722
00:26:39,430 --> 00:26:42,500
He started the conversation with,
"I'll only tell Team Red about this."

723
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:43,870
"Don't say this to anyone else."

724
00:26:43,870 --> 00:26:47,210
"Team Blue was able to produce
only two lives."

725
00:26:47,340 --> 00:26:50,140
"We won't be able to buy any lives
if they produced only two."

726
00:26:50,140 --> 00:26:51,440
This thought struck me,

727
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:52,880
and I felt very anxious at that moment.

728
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:54,510
After hearing from everyone,

729
00:26:54,510 --> 00:26:57,150
Team White doesn't want to go to war...

730
00:26:57,220 --> 00:26:59,520
until the very end.

731
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:02,020
The members of Team Blue
are busy protecting themselves.

732
00:27:02,190 --> 00:27:03,390
The members of Team Red...

733
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:07,130
were really tight with each other.

734
00:27:07,130 --> 00:27:08,560
If one of them is about to die,

735
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:09,860
I wished to make them think,

736
00:27:09,860 --> 00:27:13,730
"Won't it be more efficient to start a war
to take their lives?"

737
00:27:13,730 --> 00:27:15,470
I've set everything up.

738
00:27:15,770 --> 00:27:17,370
- The maximum is two lives.
- Right.

739
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:18,870
- Two lives for ten credits.
- Two lives?

740
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:20,710
- Two lives for ten credits.
- Isn't it better to make them get none...

741
00:27:20,710 --> 00:27:22,440
if we are to get one life?

742
00:27:22,580 --> 00:27:23,980
They must be short on credits...

743
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:25,310
for them to be desperate.

744
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:26,450
Is that what you think?

745
00:27:26,550 --> 00:27:27,810
We should go for 1 or 2.

746
00:27:27,810 --> 00:27:30,580
Let's decide after hearing about
how many they want.

747
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:31,990
"Do you need any credits?"

748
00:27:31,990 --> 00:27:33,120
If they say they don't need any,

749
00:27:33,120 --> 00:27:34,220
- should we make no trades today?
- Right.

750
00:27:34,220 --> 00:27:35,690
Let's ask them how many they want.

751
00:27:36,690 --> 00:27:38,760
Where should we talk? Here?

752
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:41,560
Isn't it too open here?

753
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,400
- We can talk quietly.
- Right.

754
00:27:43,630 --> 00:27:47,000
- Were you able to produce...
- Us?

755
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,740
- a lot today?
- We produced quite a lot.

756
00:27:48,870 --> 00:27:50,240
This team looks competent.

757
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:52,570
What's good about credits is that...

758
00:27:52,570 --> 00:27:54,570
they don't seem to be...

759
00:27:54,970 --> 00:27:56,740
that valuable to this community.

760
00:27:56,740 --> 00:27:58,750
- They aren't as valuable right now.
- Right.

761
00:27:58,750 --> 00:28:00,350
Everyone wants to avoid death.

762
00:28:00,350 --> 00:28:01,580
- Right.
- Right.

763
00:28:01,850 --> 00:28:03,550
Everything is centered around lives...

764
00:28:03,550 --> 00:28:04,820
- at this moment.
- Right.

765
00:28:04,820 --> 00:28:06,990
Do you have a good amount of lives?

766
00:28:07,050 --> 00:28:08,620
No. To be honest,

767
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:10,090
we weren't able to produce a lot today.

768
00:28:10,490 --> 00:28:11,690
We were awful.

769
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:13,960
Why? You should've used
a lot of your credits.

770
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:15,900
- We were careful with our credits.
- Right.

771
00:28:15,900 --> 00:28:17,360
We had to spend 2 to 3 credits...

772
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:19,470
- to earn one life.
- I see.

773
00:28:19,470 --> 00:28:21,730
Nothing has changed from yesterday.

774
00:28:21,730 --> 00:28:23,740
- As for today...
- You must...

775
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:25,240
produce a lot of lives.

776
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,810
Right. You must produce a lot...

777
00:28:26,810 --> 00:28:28,510
- to maintain this peace.
- Right.

778
00:28:28,510 --> 00:28:30,980
- The moment you fail to do so,
- Lives are crucial right now.

779
00:28:30,980 --> 00:28:33,380
it will be the start of a war.

780
00:28:33,380 --> 00:28:35,210
If we are to avoid going to war...

781
00:28:35,210 --> 00:28:36,780
and live as a community,

782
00:28:36,780 --> 00:28:39,750
we need to make sacrifices
with each other...

783
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:41,920
or reach an agreement.

784
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:43,690
If that's not the case,

785
00:28:43,690 --> 00:28:46,230
we will work for ourselves...

786
00:28:46,230 --> 00:28:48,560
and end up going to war.

787
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:51,860
To be honest, we aren't sure...

788
00:28:51,860 --> 00:28:54,170
which direction to take.

789
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:56,040
- I see.
- Right.

790
00:28:58,540 --> 00:28:59,570
Not at all.

791
00:29:01,870 --> 00:29:04,140
- Why are they fighting so much?
- They must be going to war.

792
00:29:04,180 --> 00:29:05,580
Gosh.

793
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:07,310
It feels like they're about to go to war.

794
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:09,020
- It's like it's going to happen now.
- Right.

795
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:10,380
I did my best...

796
00:29:10,380 --> 00:29:13,190
to stop them from going to war.

797
00:29:13,290 --> 00:29:14,750
I thought about this.

798
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,990
I think my role is Switzerland.

799
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:18,520
- A neutral country.
- A neutral country?

800
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:21,330
That is why I'm excluded from
going to war.

801
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:23,560
Right. That would be too much
of a disadvantage for you.

802
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:26,170
I am to be a trader while maintaining
friendly relationships with everyone.

803
00:29:26,670 --> 00:29:28,500
That's by selling things.

804
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,270
My mission is to...

805
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:31,700
get items handed over to me...

806
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:33,840
and to earn my prize money
by selling them.

807
00:29:34,910 --> 00:29:36,310
Black is...

808
00:29:36,310 --> 00:29:38,640
my only smoking buddy,

809
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:39,880
but I can't trust him at all.

810
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:42,080
When someone looks determined and smart,

811
00:29:42,080 --> 00:29:44,450
they have a greater goal.

812
00:29:44,450 --> 00:29:47,420
There's a big chance
that he's hiding something.

813
00:29:47,490 --> 00:29:49,390
When I went on a different survival show,

814
00:29:49,390 --> 00:29:52,590
I got duped by everyone who looked nice.

815
00:29:52,730 --> 00:29:54,930
I got duped so many times.

816
00:29:54,930 --> 00:29:57,730
I was an expert at getting duped.

817
00:29:57,730 --> 00:29:59,570
While playing a fool,

818
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:02,740
I am determined to...

819
00:30:02,740 --> 00:30:04,070
go after my target.

820
00:30:04,170 --> 00:30:08,410
Paul seems to trust Black.

821
00:30:08,410 --> 00:30:10,080
Black will try to dupe Paul,

822
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:11,210
but Paul will dupe him instead.

823
00:30:11,340 --> 00:30:12,780
Black is on his own.

824
00:30:12,780 --> 00:30:15,980
He has a very vague role.

825
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,250
He seems to be an almighty being,

826
00:30:18,250 --> 00:30:20,950
but he's also someone who can't do much.

827
00:30:21,050 --> 00:30:23,020
He had such a neutral role.

828
00:30:23,020 --> 00:30:25,190
I kept my guard up...

829
00:30:25,190 --> 00:30:26,960
as he could get us from behind
at any moment.

830
00:30:27,030 --> 00:30:28,290
I have a question.

831
00:30:28,290 --> 00:30:30,860
It's quite obvious that the team
to be with Team White will win.

832
00:30:31,230 --> 00:30:33,000
- It'll be 9 against 3.
- Right.

833
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,700
It'll be one or the other.

834
00:30:34,700 --> 00:30:36,300
Which side will you favor more?

835
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:37,900
We will seek peace.

836
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:39,040
- Peace is our priority.
- Your mind is set?

837
00:30:39,040 --> 00:30:40,140
No alliances?

838
00:30:40,140 --> 00:30:41,840
- It's because...
- That will be inevitable, but...

839
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:44,210
No one will ever try to fight
against nine.

840
00:30:45,140 --> 00:30:47,610
There's a big chance...

841
00:30:47,610 --> 00:30:51,180
that the 3 who go against 9
will get destroyed.

842
00:30:51,180 --> 00:30:53,090
I believe it's important for us...

843
00:30:53,090 --> 00:30:55,890
to maintain friendly relationships.

844
00:30:55,990 --> 00:30:57,920
- We want to keep things peaceful.
- Right.

845
00:30:58,220 --> 00:30:59,660
As for Team White,

846
00:30:59,660 --> 00:31:02,900
the value of diamonds went up by a lot...

847
00:31:02,900 --> 00:31:04,730
after the announcement of war.

848
00:31:04,860 --> 00:31:07,130
Even without my help,

849
00:31:07,130 --> 00:31:09,670
they were making good deals.

850
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:13,610
I thought hard about how to make them
go to war.

851
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:16,540
If I want a war to start,

852
00:31:16,540 --> 00:31:18,810
I should make the fee for war
very affordable.

853
00:31:19,050 --> 00:31:21,180
I should make them think,

854
00:31:21,180 --> 00:31:22,780
"Should we go to war?"

855
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:25,450
Once the members of Team White
start getting wiped out,

856
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:28,350
a more balanced war will be available.

857
00:31:28,350 --> 00:31:29,460
I believe I can...

858
00:31:29,460 --> 00:31:32,020
aim after Team White when that happens.

859
00:31:32,930 --> 00:31:35,460
To maintain peace,

860
00:31:35,460 --> 00:31:37,430
we must each make some sacrifices.

861
00:31:37,430 --> 00:31:38,530
- But...
- It would be better...

862
00:31:38,530 --> 00:31:40,100
to give out more credits.

863
00:31:40,100 --> 00:31:42,130
We must provide more...

864
00:31:42,130 --> 00:31:44,500
- for Team Blue to produce more.
- Right.

865
00:31:44,700 --> 00:31:46,670
This is what I'm curious about.

866
00:31:47,570 --> 00:31:50,040
Are you able to sell lives at this point?

867
00:31:50,110 --> 00:31:54,380
As of right now,

868
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:56,420
we aren't short on credits.

869
00:31:56,420 --> 00:31:57,550
Do you not need...

870
00:31:57,550 --> 00:31:58,720
any credits right now?

871
00:31:58,750 --> 00:32:00,590
That's not it!

872
00:32:00,820 --> 00:32:02,360
- That sounded so cold.
- No.

873
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:04,190
- That's not true.
- I was told that credits weren't needed.

874
00:32:04,190 --> 00:32:06,030
- That's not it.
- This is what it's like.

875
00:32:06,030 --> 00:32:08,060
It's not that credits aren't needed.

876
00:32:08,060 --> 00:32:09,800
- We...
- We really want them,

877
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:10,900
- We want them...
- but here's nothing we can do.

878
00:32:10,900 --> 00:32:12,430
Since you can't offer anything,

879
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,400
- so you can't ask for anything?
- Yes.

880
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:15,870
- Exactly.
- We'd appreciate it...

881
00:32:15,870 --> 00:32:18,000
if you gave us some, but it's not like...

882
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,670
we have no shame.

883
00:32:19,970 --> 00:32:20,970
True.

884
00:32:20,970 --> 00:32:22,780
Even from my perspective,

885
00:32:22,780 --> 00:32:25,510
credits may not be
that useful at the moment.

886
00:32:25,510 --> 00:32:28,010
But when making necessary trades...

887
00:32:28,010 --> 00:32:30,220
and doing productive activities,
credits are a must.

888
00:32:30,480 --> 00:32:32,350
Underestimate credits,

889
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:34,590
and we might all go down together.

890
00:32:35,320 --> 00:32:38,390
Honestly, all the teams are in the green.

891
00:32:38,390 --> 00:32:40,390
Let's see how much we produce tomorrow...

892
00:32:40,390 --> 00:32:42,460
- and talk again.
- But to produce enough tomorrow,

893
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:44,000
- don't you need credits right now?
- True.

894
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,130
- Like, as a bit of backup.
- It'd be nice if we did.

895
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:48,130
To be frank, we were very prudent...

896
00:32:48,130 --> 00:32:50,000
about using credits today...

897
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:52,270
- as we didn't have many.
- I thought so.

898
00:32:52,710 --> 00:32:54,070
Credits are useful.

899
00:32:54,210 --> 00:32:56,240
Our team used a handful of them today.

900
00:32:56,580 --> 00:32:57,810
We also produced a lot.

901
00:32:58,040 --> 00:33:00,310
But here's the thing.
Even if we were to use credits,

902
00:33:00,310 --> 00:33:02,380
- we'd need basic knowledge.
- True.

903
00:33:02,380 --> 00:33:03,520
It's hard to grasp without it.

904
00:33:03,520 --> 00:33:05,180
Don't say it. It's making me feel small.

905
00:33:05,180 --> 00:33:06,750
- But...
- I know.

906
00:33:06,750 --> 00:33:09,660
We got several questions from hints.

907
00:33:09,920 --> 00:33:11,360
The best is...

908
00:33:12,730 --> 00:33:15,360
Thirty minutes left of trading.

909
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:18,130
I'm feeling very anxious.

910
00:33:18,730 --> 00:33:20,270
I'll go give them a heads-up about...

911
00:33:20,270 --> 00:33:21,800
- the trade with us.
- Okay.

912
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,300
- If so...
- Excuse me.

913
00:33:24,300 --> 00:33:26,410
- Yes?
- I won't join your conversation.

914
00:33:26,410 --> 00:33:27,470
Our teams need to trade,

915
00:33:27,470 --> 00:33:29,010
- but the remaining time...
- Right.

916
00:33:29,010 --> 00:33:30,740
We also need to make a trade
with every team,

917
00:33:30,740 --> 00:33:32,210
- so we'll rush it.
- We'll be there in a bit.

918
00:33:32,210 --> 00:33:33,950
- We'll be there in five minutes.
- Okay.

919
00:33:33,950 --> 00:33:36,920
Will it be impossible to solve
even 1 or 2 questions?

920
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:39,350
We'll be in a worse deficit
than yesterday.

921
00:33:39,620 --> 00:33:41,220
- Then...
- What do we do?

922
00:33:41,220 --> 00:33:42,760
- We...
- Can we make free exchanges?

923
00:33:42,760 --> 00:33:45,360
- Exchanges?
- If you don't use the credits now,

924
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:46,630
- you can't use them...
- They must have...

925
00:33:46,630 --> 00:33:48,290
- tomorrow either, right?
- enough for tomorrow.

926
00:33:48,630 --> 00:33:49,930
- But you see,
- Yes?

927
00:33:50,430 --> 00:33:53,400
- Team Blue should get some credits.
- You want to give them some?

928
00:33:54,430 --> 00:33:56,370
If we could get even just one life,

929
00:33:56,370 --> 00:33:59,340
I wanted to use credits
to set sail tomorrow.

930
00:34:03,140 --> 00:34:04,710
Waiting for another day isn't that bad.

931
00:34:04,710 --> 00:34:07,150
But that just feels like wasting a day.

932
00:34:07,150 --> 00:34:09,720
- Give us time to think about it,
- If things get worse...

933
00:34:09,720 --> 00:34:11,920
so if you were to give us
an offer first...

934
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:13,920
- Say that we overdo ourselves.
- Okay.

935
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,920
We overdo ourselves
and distribute something.

936
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:17,490
How many credits are you willing to trade?

937
00:34:18,160 --> 00:34:19,290
Eight.

938
00:34:19,290 --> 00:34:20,460
- Eight?
- Yes.

939
00:34:21,090 --> 00:34:22,090
Sorry?

940
00:34:22,090 --> 00:34:23,130
(Maillard's offer)

941
00:34:23,130 --> 00:34:24,530
Eight credits for one life.

942
00:34:24,530 --> 00:34:27,030
Is that telling them to go all-in
and earn lives tomorrow?

943
00:34:27,030 --> 00:34:28,570
Isn't it a little too unfair?

944
00:34:28,570 --> 00:34:30,040
It's way too good for us.

945
00:34:30,470 --> 00:34:32,200
- The thing is...
- Why worry about that?

946
00:34:32,710 --> 00:34:34,740
- Honestly, right now, we're almost...
- It's not a 1-on-1 trade.

947
00:34:34,740 --> 00:34:36,580
- It's just...
- This is for the whole economy.

948
00:34:36,580 --> 00:34:38,710
- It's practically...
- Think of it as preventing war.

949
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:40,080
- Exactly.
- Were we that bad today?

950
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,180
- I...
- Without any lives,

951
00:34:41,180 --> 00:34:44,320
- all of us are in grave trouble.
- I seriously want to crawl under a rock.

952
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:47,190
- But listen. If we were able to get...
- Yes?

953
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:48,720
- resources in advance and did so.
- Okay.

954
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:51,020
- We saw the hint.
- Okay.

955
00:34:51,020 --> 00:34:52,660
But if we fail to answer anything...

956
00:34:52,660 --> 00:34:54,190
We need to cross the line.
That'll improve our chances,

957
00:34:54,190 --> 00:34:56,160
- and I mean our overall chances.
- The chances increase.

958
00:34:56,160 --> 00:34:57,400
- Let's grow the market.
- Then...

959
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:59,830
- First...
- Whether we don't get the answer...

960
00:34:59,830 --> 00:35:01,270
because we have no credits
or even with credits,

961
00:35:01,270 --> 00:35:03,340
the result is the same
if we don't get the answer tomorrow.

962
00:35:03,340 --> 00:35:04,340
- The deal...
- We need to cross the line.

963
00:35:04,340 --> 00:35:06,340
- Whether we make a deal or not,
- What now?

964
00:35:06,340 --> 00:35:08,110
we're out of time.

965
00:35:08,110 --> 00:35:09,610
- For now, let's get moving.
- Okay.

966
00:35:09,610 --> 00:35:10,710
Regardless of whether we do it or not,

967
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:12,110
- we will bring it over.
- We'll bring ours too.

968
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:13,580
- No, let's meet there.
- Right.

969
00:35:13,580 --> 00:35:15,010
- We'll meet you there.
- Okay, we'll meet you there.

970
00:35:15,010 --> 00:35:16,320
- Right.
- We'll bring ours too.

971
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,880
- We'd better hurry.
- Right.

972
00:35:18,820 --> 00:35:20,550
Do we have enough to spare, like one?

973
00:35:20,550 --> 00:35:22,820
Trading 1 life for 8 credits is
a very generous offer.

974
00:35:22,820 --> 00:35:24,320
True, I agree.

975
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:26,060
I didn't expect them to be that generous.

976
00:35:26,060 --> 00:35:28,730
- They...
- But they realized it too that...

977
00:35:28,730 --> 00:35:32,100
- Right.
- yesterday's deal was a total jackpot.

978
00:35:32,100 --> 00:35:34,400
Either way, their goal seems to be
to find the exact value...

979
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:36,040
and increase the resources,

980
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,670
not to chip away at us...

981
00:35:37,670 --> 00:35:39,140
or be all calculative about losses.

982
00:35:39,140 --> 00:35:41,870
Producing lives is extremely important...

983
00:35:41,870 --> 00:35:43,380
- right now.
- They're being smart.

984
00:35:43,810 --> 00:35:46,080
When we do something,

985
00:35:46,080 --> 00:35:48,010
like using the hint,

986
00:35:48,010 --> 00:35:50,680
- we barely have any credits.
- True.

987
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:51,680
Do we agree to the offer?

988
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:53,320
- Yes.
- Even if we negotiate?

989
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,790
- Yes.
- It's such a generous offer,

990
00:35:54,790 --> 00:35:56,090
which I really think we should accept.

991
00:35:56,360 --> 00:35:59,390
- All we can offer is five.
- Yes?

992
00:35:59,560 --> 00:36:01,290
The other team gets five,

993
00:36:01,290 --> 00:36:02,960
- and so do we?
- Correct.

994
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:06,570
Your deal with the other team
didn't cancel, right?

995
00:36:06,570 --> 00:36:08,870
The deal hasn't been set in stone yet.

996
00:36:09,100 --> 00:36:12,240
Honestly, they had nothing to offer.
But we...

997
00:36:12,240 --> 00:36:13,810
If they're not in,

998
00:36:13,810 --> 00:36:15,980
we don't have a deal with Team Blue today.

999
00:36:16,140 --> 00:36:18,380
If your deal with Team Blue falls through,

1000
00:36:18,380 --> 00:36:21,910
is there a way
we could get those credits instead?

1001
00:36:24,150 --> 00:36:26,390
The thing is, if the deal with
Team Blue falls apart,

1002
00:36:26,690 --> 00:36:28,390
it'll be bad for all of us.

1003
00:36:28,550 --> 00:36:31,720
Only when we give some help to
Team Blue with...

1004
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,790
- some credits...
- It's our way of supporting them.

1005
00:36:33,790 --> 00:36:35,690
We have to raise Team Blue together.

1006
00:36:35,930 --> 00:36:38,460
- That's what we also want.
- Great.

1007
00:36:38,460 --> 00:36:40,600
- But if it doesn't go as planned,
- If it doesn't go as planned...

1008
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:42,330
- we might want more credits.
- Got it.

1009
00:36:42,330 --> 00:36:43,870
- We'll even cheer you on from the side.
- Okay.

1010
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:47,010
- I'll go bring our credits.
- Okay, go ahead.

1011
00:36:48,110 --> 00:36:49,340
There has to be something.

1012
00:36:49,340 --> 00:36:50,710
- Are you in on it?
- We are.

1013
00:36:50,780 --> 00:36:51,780
Got it.

1014
00:36:51,780 --> 00:36:53,010
Don't tell the quantity to the other team.

1015
00:36:53,010 --> 00:36:54,210
- Got it.
- Of course not.

1016
00:36:54,450 --> 00:36:55,450
Run.

1017
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:57,750
I know how hard that is,
so I can't let the offer go.

1018
00:36:58,450 --> 00:37:00,320
Running up those stairs is not easy.
It's tough.

1019
00:37:03,260 --> 00:37:09,560
(A fierce determination
to raise Team Blue)

1020
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,110
(Out of the 29,)

1021
00:37:21,110 --> 00:37:24,140
(Maillard takes 13 with him.)

1022
00:37:24,610 --> 00:37:25,710
The time...

1023
00:37:26,310 --> 00:37:27,750
- The time is...
- Well...

1024
00:37:27,750 --> 00:37:29,280
- Everyone, the time is...
- It won't take long.

1025
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,480
Do you mind if we quickly trade first?

1026
00:37:30,480 --> 00:37:31,780
- Go ahead.
- Sure.

1027
00:37:31,780 --> 00:37:33,350
- We'll be back fast.
- Be careful.

1028
00:37:33,650 --> 00:37:34,650
Peacefully, you know?

1029
00:37:34,650 --> 00:37:36,190
Let's be quick, okay?

1030
00:37:36,190 --> 00:37:37,890
(Maillard's offer)

1031
00:37:37,890 --> 00:37:41,990
Who will be paying the credits
to make this trade?

1032
00:37:41,990 --> 00:37:43,760
We came in without discussing that.

1033
00:37:44,430 --> 00:37:46,870
- Our team will pay for it for now.
- Okay, got it.

1034
00:37:46,970 --> 00:37:48,700
The trade has been completed.

1035
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:51,570
Please collect the resources and exit.

1036
00:37:51,570 --> 00:37:52,570
(1 life)

1037
00:37:53,040 --> 00:37:54,940
One, two, three, four...

1038
00:37:54,940 --> 00:37:57,340
(Traded with 7 credits)

1039
00:37:57,340 --> 00:37:58,780
- Thank you.
- I've collected them.

1040
00:37:59,140 --> 00:38:01,650
- Please produce a lot tomorrow.
- Okay.

1041
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,880
- We'll be rooting for you.
- I'll study before going to bed tonight.

1042
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,720
For your information, the disease book...

1043
00:38:06,720 --> 00:38:08,090
- Yes?
- was used today.

1044
00:38:08,090 --> 00:38:09,920
- Is the hint really...
- It's in there.

1045
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,390
- in the book?
- The answer is in there.

1046
00:38:11,390 --> 00:38:13,460
The thing is, our books differ.

1047
00:38:13,460 --> 00:38:14,490
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1048
00:38:14,930 --> 00:38:16,160
Anyway, we used the disease book.

1049
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:18,260
I'd better look at the books thoroughly.

1050
00:38:18,660 --> 00:38:20,600
(Teams White and Red trade next.)

1051
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:22,570
So you used the disease book.

1052
00:38:22,570 --> 00:38:24,570
It would be nice...

1053
00:38:24,570 --> 00:38:27,670
if we shared the themes...

1054
00:38:27,670 --> 00:38:29,070
- of our books.
- Right?

1055
00:38:29,310 --> 00:38:31,540
The Trading Station has been activated.

1056
00:38:32,210 --> 00:38:34,150
(10 diamonds)

1057
00:38:34,150 --> 00:38:35,180
Four.

1058
00:38:35,180 --> 00:38:36,550
(4 credits)

1059
00:38:36,920 --> 00:38:38,650
- Four and ten. Correct?
- Yes.

1060
00:38:41,090 --> 00:38:42,350
All done.

1061
00:38:42,350 --> 00:38:46,460
We're checking the submitted amount.
Please wait a moment.

1062
00:38:51,030 --> 00:38:53,800
Does Team White also appoint the leader
every morning?

1063
00:38:54,030 --> 00:38:55,570
- Yes, we did this morning.
- You did?

1064
00:38:55,570 --> 00:38:56,570
Yes.

1065
00:38:56,570 --> 00:38:58,800
How's it being the leader?

1066
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:00,210
I thought there'd be a benefit,

1067
00:39:00,210 --> 00:39:02,370
like a life I could use alone.

1068
00:39:02,370 --> 00:39:03,580
- Right?
- But there's nothing.

1069
00:39:03,580 --> 00:39:05,410
Maybe it helps improve our stamina.

1070
00:39:10,550 --> 00:39:13,120
But there's this one perk.

1071
00:39:13,350 --> 00:39:16,090
Before going to bed,
if I were to just lose it,

1072
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:20,460
- Kill everyone out of the blue?
- kill everyone besides myself.

1073
00:39:21,390 --> 00:39:23,030
What if you lose it for real?

1074
00:39:23,030 --> 00:39:25,160
It's kind of like
socially killing yourself.

1075
00:39:35,210 --> 00:39:37,110
The trade has been completed.

1076
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:39,410
Please collect the resources and exit.

1077
00:39:51,820 --> 00:39:54,690
(Teams White and Red are done trading.)

1078
00:39:54,690 --> 00:39:56,060
- Good work.
- Someone's carrying money...

1079
00:39:56,060 --> 00:39:57,060
in their pocket.

1080
00:39:57,400 --> 00:39:59,100
- It's just that...
- Each is worth 1,000 dollars.

1081
00:40:00,270 --> 00:40:02,500
- It's easy to carry around.
- Don't lose it, okay?

1082
00:40:02,500 --> 00:40:03,870
It's priceless.

1083
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:06,740
- They didn't take long.
- Good work.

1084
00:40:06,740 --> 00:40:08,540
- Good work.
- Good work.

1085
00:40:08,540 --> 00:40:11,140
- We made it in time.
- Peace has come to everyone.

1086
00:40:11,540 --> 00:40:13,210
- We got through the day.
- Nice.

1087
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:15,680
- Good work.
- Good work.

1088
00:40:16,350 --> 00:40:20,450
How the game unfolded today was
somewhat satisfactory.

1089
00:40:20,650 --> 00:40:23,220
Team Blue kept the alliance of 9-to-3.

1090
00:40:23,460 --> 00:40:26,590
What was promised was 2,
but they gave us 3.

1091
00:40:26,730 --> 00:40:30,530
"When something happens,
we have to be together."

1092
00:40:30,530 --> 00:40:33,670
We gave each other such trust.

1093
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:37,140
Of course, I still have my guard up,

1094
00:40:37,140 --> 00:40:40,270
but as long as
it's in their best interest, I trust them.

1095
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:42,210
It's hard to believe that...

1096
00:40:42,210 --> 00:40:45,140
they only produced two lives today.

1097
00:40:45,140 --> 00:40:46,810
We put it strongly today.

1098
00:40:46,980 --> 00:40:49,950
"Use your hints and such
to produce as many lives as possible,"

1099
00:40:50,450 --> 00:40:53,820
"so that we can find a way
for all of us to survive tomorrow."

1100
00:40:54,090 --> 00:40:56,720
I'm hoping that
they'll get the answers right.

1101
00:40:57,060 --> 00:40:59,830
I believe we're being too conservative,

1102
00:40:59,830 --> 00:41:01,460
which is frustrating.

1103
00:41:01,860 --> 00:41:04,530
We currently have many lives in storage.

1104
00:41:04,530 --> 00:41:07,870
It could leave them feeling
a sense of loss.

1105
00:41:07,870 --> 00:41:10,500
Until today, they kept saying,

1106
00:41:10,500 --> 00:41:13,070
"You must survive."

1107
00:41:13,070 --> 00:41:14,270
"You're indispensable."

1108
00:41:14,270 --> 00:41:15,510
But behind our backs,

1109
00:41:15,510 --> 00:41:19,680
they would definitely be like,
"You can live another 2 to 3 days."

1110
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:23,650
"You totally can, but you're not willing
to trade them?"

1111
00:41:23,650 --> 00:41:25,920
When such a feeling of loss emerges,

1112
00:41:25,920 --> 00:41:27,550
war can break out.

1113
00:41:27,550 --> 00:41:30,360
"As the leader,
I can just dogmatically hurt them."

1114
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:33,160
When such thoughts crossed my mind
every now and then,

1115
00:41:33,160 --> 00:41:35,760
I couldn't make that choice in the end.

1116
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,260
Why is being a leader so tough?

1117
00:41:37,430 --> 00:41:39,360
I want to quit being one already.

1118
00:41:39,870 --> 00:41:43,040
Mining the resources is
much harder than expected.

1119
00:41:43,240 --> 00:41:47,270
Even so,
the market is filled with lives now.

1120
00:41:47,270 --> 00:41:49,480
It worries me. Only when...

1121
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:52,140
there aren't enough lives
will people feel the pinch...

1122
00:41:52,140 --> 00:41:53,750
and start a war.

1123
00:41:54,110 --> 00:41:55,610
"It won't be easy until Day Two."

1124
00:41:55,610 --> 00:41:56,980
That was what I thought.

1125
00:41:56,980 --> 00:42:00,150
"Suddenly starting a war on Day Two
isn't easy."

1126
00:42:00,390 --> 00:42:02,350
"If the productive activity is tough,"

1127
00:42:02,350 --> 00:42:05,190
"Day Three might be hopeful,"
was what I thought.

1128
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:09,130
We have to mine at least two lives
to survive until the day after tomorrow.

1129
00:42:09,130 --> 00:42:10,500
At this rate,

1130
00:42:10,500 --> 00:42:12,060
because of the two that Team Blue earned,

1131
00:42:12,060 --> 00:42:13,830
- we're all stalled.
- Exactly.

1132
00:42:13,830 --> 00:42:16,740
Our economy has stagnated.
It's not flowing.

1133
00:42:16,900 --> 00:42:18,540
Will everyone survive today?

1134
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:21,310
Here's the only elimination scenario.

1135
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:23,010
- The leader's betrayal.
- Exactly.

1136
00:42:23,010 --> 00:42:24,080
That's the only case.

1137
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:27,480
But will these two betray the others?

1138
00:42:28,350 --> 00:42:31,420
I think Luna should make up her mind.

1139
00:42:31,420 --> 00:42:33,320
- By getting rid of three people,
- That?

1140
00:42:33,820 --> 00:42:35,020
she could last quite a while.

1141
00:42:35,020 --> 00:42:36,290
Her chances double.

1142
00:42:36,290 --> 00:42:37,890
Right? It's four days' worth.

1143
00:42:37,890 --> 00:42:39,490
- What's more...
- Four days' worth in one go.

1144
00:42:39,630 --> 00:42:40,930
There's a limited amount of supply,

1145
00:42:40,930 --> 00:42:43,160
so that could be
how we can survive together.

1146
00:42:43,730 --> 00:42:45,630
Should I ask her quietly today?

1147
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:48,770
For everyone's eternal life,
get rid of some people.

1148
00:42:48,930 --> 00:42:52,200
We could help eliminate
the members of Team White.

1149
00:42:52,770 --> 00:42:54,040
Internal conflict will arise.

1150
00:42:55,340 --> 00:42:58,210
We do have
an overwhelming number of diamonds.

1151
00:42:58,210 --> 00:43:00,210
We'd better be careful
because if we say we barely have any,

1152
00:43:00,210 --> 00:43:02,150
we'd be deceiving.

1153
00:43:03,250 --> 00:43:05,880
Should we eat today?

1154
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:08,650
Because it feels like
there's no money circulating.

1155
00:43:08,650 --> 00:43:10,790
Should we release a few...

1156
00:43:10,790 --> 00:43:12,760
by buying food?

1157
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:13,760
But...

1158
00:43:14,060 --> 00:43:16,560
if we give it to Team Black,
it's not going to circulate anyway.

1159
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:17,960
He's taking them to himself.

1160
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:19,900
- But it looks like...
- So there's no point of spending any.

1161
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:25,000
they're all thinking about something good
for the public.

1162
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:26,810
It's not for the public.

1163
00:43:26,810 --> 00:43:30,040
They're begging those with lives
to survive.

1164
00:43:30,380 --> 00:43:32,640
We have no reason to give them diamonds...

1165
00:43:32,640 --> 00:43:34,310
when we're already eating our lives away.

1166
00:43:34,310 --> 00:43:37,050
Unless we're going there...

1167
00:43:37,050 --> 00:43:38,150
to eat fried chicken and pork belly...

1168
00:43:38,150 --> 00:43:40,420
- like crazy,
- So...

1169
00:43:40,420 --> 00:43:42,390
we're paying only one diamond...

1170
00:43:42,390 --> 00:43:44,290
for one bagel. That's about it.

1171
00:43:44,290 --> 00:43:46,260
So what's the point?

1172
00:43:46,460 --> 00:43:48,760
There still is a point.

1173
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:50,700
- There is a point.
- There is a point, but...

1174
00:43:50,700 --> 00:43:52,800
- I get what you mean.
- If that's the reason,

1175
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:55,070
we've talked about pizza, eggs,

1176
00:43:55,070 --> 00:43:56,300
and soya milk already.

1177
00:43:56,300 --> 00:44:00,070
If we say we bought food,

1178
00:44:00,070 --> 00:44:01,810
they'd think we only spent a few.

1179
00:44:01,810 --> 00:44:06,140
So if we end up spending 2 or 3 more
to show them,

1180
00:44:06,140 --> 00:44:08,680
they'll think, "They must've spent 5.
They must've spent 7."

1181
00:44:08,680 --> 00:44:09,850
It makes no difference.

1182
00:44:12,180 --> 00:44:14,050
To be honest,

1183
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:17,590
I don't want to spend diamonds on food.

1184
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:20,630
Okay. We agreed...

1185
00:44:20,630 --> 00:44:22,360
to respect each other.

1186
00:44:25,860 --> 00:44:27,500
It's dinner time.

1187
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:32,340
Please have dinner in the Town Hall.

1188
00:44:33,210 --> 00:44:34,210
(The Town Hall is still empty.)

1189
00:44:34,210 --> 00:44:35,370
Even for him.

1190
00:44:35,370 --> 00:44:36,680
I thought it was dinner time.

1191
00:44:36,680 --> 00:44:38,910
We already chose what to eat.

1192
00:44:38,910 --> 00:44:40,550
We can just microwave it, right?

1193
00:44:41,610 --> 00:44:44,780
(Team Blue saved pizza during lunch.)

1194
00:44:44,780 --> 00:44:45,880
How long do we microwave it?

1195
00:44:46,250 --> 00:44:47,620
Eight to nine minutes.

1196
00:44:48,790 --> 00:44:49,790
He's here.

1197
00:44:50,860 --> 00:44:52,520
Where is everyone?

1198
00:44:52,520 --> 00:44:53,530
I think they're coming.

1199
00:44:53,530 --> 00:44:55,530
If no one's here yet,
should we give it to him now?

1200
00:44:55,890 --> 00:44:57,260
- Sounds good.
- Yes.

1201
00:44:59,130 --> 00:45:01,570
(They hid 1 life...)

1202
00:45:01,570 --> 00:45:02,870
Will it fit in here?

1203
00:45:02,870 --> 00:45:03,870
(in the glass case
for black-market deals.)

1204
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:06,570
- You should...
- Take it...

1205
00:45:06,570 --> 00:45:08,010
- when there's no one.
- And...

1206
00:45:08,010 --> 00:45:10,180
It's the payment for the pizza.

1207
00:45:10,180 --> 00:45:11,180
Okay.

1208
00:45:12,380 --> 00:45:13,810
You already opened it.

1209
00:45:13,810 --> 00:45:15,510
On credit.

1210
00:45:19,890 --> 00:45:22,750
(Although it's given to Team Black,)

1211
00:45:22,750 --> 00:45:25,320
(the amount of resources doesn't change.)

1212
00:45:27,690 --> 00:45:28,790
Can you...

1213
00:45:28,790 --> 00:45:30,130
tell us...

1214
00:45:30,130 --> 00:45:32,200
- just in case...
- Things you took?

1215
00:45:32,200 --> 00:45:34,830
- Yes.
- Say you paid 2 for 1 egg and that.

1216
00:45:34,830 --> 00:45:36,570
Three eggs and one pizza.

1217
00:45:36,940 --> 00:45:38,570
- One pizza?
- Yes.

1218
00:45:38,570 --> 00:45:39,770
But they wouldn't ask.

1219
00:45:39,770 --> 00:45:40,970
It's a secret.

1220
00:45:41,910 --> 00:45:43,380
- Hello.
- You're very early.

1221
00:45:43,380 --> 00:45:45,910
- Yes. We were hungry.
- I can see that.

1222
00:45:45,910 --> 00:45:47,250
What do you want to eat?

1223
00:45:47,250 --> 00:45:48,680
What do you want? The lunchbox?

1224
00:45:48,680 --> 00:45:49,980
How much is the fried chicken?

1225
00:45:49,980 --> 00:45:52,020
I need at least two for that.

1226
00:45:52,020 --> 00:45:53,050
It's chicken.

1227
00:45:53,050 --> 00:45:54,820
The fried chicken deserves two.

1228
00:45:54,820 --> 00:45:56,590
- How about we have one?
- You'll have one?

1229
00:45:56,590 --> 00:45:57,660
- Half and half?
- Half and half, please.

1230
00:45:57,660 --> 00:45:58,660
Okay.

1231
00:45:58,660 --> 00:46:00,560
Everyone.
There are only two fried chickens left.

1232
00:46:00,560 --> 00:46:01,760
There are only two fried chickens left.

1233
00:46:01,760 --> 00:46:02,890
- There are only two fried chickens left.
- That's his gimmick.

1234
00:46:02,890 --> 00:46:03,960
That's his gimmick.

1235
00:46:03,960 --> 00:46:05,260
Oh, thank you.

1236
00:46:05,260 --> 00:46:07,100
- Nice.
- For the fried chicken.

1237
00:46:07,100 --> 00:46:08,630
It's worth 2,000 dollars.

1238
00:46:08,630 --> 00:46:11,000
- It's worth 2,000 dollars.
- A chicken worth 2,000 dollars.

1239
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:14,070
We traded a life for food.

1240
00:46:14,070 --> 00:46:15,640
Yet, she wants to give him diamonds.

1241
00:46:15,640 --> 00:46:17,910
I don't see the point.

1242
00:46:17,910 --> 00:46:21,080
The idea of surviving together.

1243
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:24,080
How others see us
and what they think of us.

1244
00:46:24,080 --> 00:46:26,220
She cares about that so much.

1245
00:46:26,720 --> 00:46:29,890
I kept thinking, "That isn't the point."

1246
00:46:30,060 --> 00:46:32,160
Let me have the meat dumplings.

1247
00:46:32,160 --> 00:46:33,660
I'll have an egg and soya milk.

1248
00:46:33,660 --> 00:46:35,460
- It's healthy.
- Very healthy.

1249
00:46:35,460 --> 00:46:36,600
- It's all protein.
- Yes.

1250
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:38,100
Today, I'll make it a combo...

1251
00:46:38,100 --> 00:46:40,130
and give you a fried chicken for five.

1252
00:46:40,130 --> 00:46:43,300
Five for all this and a fried chicken?

1253
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:45,370
- Really?
- We can always order more later.

1254
00:46:45,370 --> 00:46:46,970
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1255
00:46:46,970 --> 00:46:48,010
Thank you.

1256
00:46:48,010 --> 00:46:50,840
Do you want to have ramyeon and dumplings?

1257
00:46:51,010 --> 00:46:52,010
Sure.

1258
00:46:52,110 --> 00:46:54,380
(Team Red picks up the food they had.)

1259
00:46:54,380 --> 00:46:55,380
Let's go.

1260
00:46:55,610 --> 00:46:57,650
Is Team Red not eating?

1261
00:46:57,920 --> 00:47:00,990
Is Team Red preparing for a war?

1262
00:47:01,550 --> 00:47:03,120
We're late.

1263
00:47:03,390 --> 00:47:04,390
Sorry.

1264
00:47:04,390 --> 00:47:06,730
Oh, they don't need to buy anything
for dinner.

1265
00:47:06,730 --> 00:47:07,930
What?

1266
00:47:07,930 --> 00:47:09,330
- They're rich.
- We bought it earlier.

1267
00:47:09,330 --> 00:47:12,130
I have to sell ramyeon,
but they brought ramyeon.

1268
00:47:13,030 --> 00:47:14,800
- Come on.
- No more ramyeon sales today.

1269
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:16,970
I'm doomed. I'm so bad at sales.

1270
00:47:18,700 --> 00:47:20,840
When did you order the fried chicken?

1271
00:47:21,170 --> 00:47:23,010
About 15 to 20 minutes? Maybe?

1272
00:47:23,010 --> 00:47:26,240
I have a feeling you can guess the time.

1273
00:47:26,240 --> 00:47:28,510
- No.
- Are you an athlete?

1274
00:47:28,510 --> 00:47:30,520
- What did you do?
- Kind of. I was a soldier.

1275
00:47:30,520 --> 00:47:32,220
- A soldier?
- Now,

1276
00:47:32,220 --> 00:47:33,590
I'm in the bomb disposal unit.

1277
00:47:33,590 --> 00:47:35,120
That's scary.

1278
00:47:35,120 --> 00:47:37,160
I'm so proud of you.

1279
00:47:38,020 --> 00:47:39,420
Even though that's not what I do,

1280
00:47:39,420 --> 00:47:41,530
- It's reassuring.
- we're on the same team.

1281
00:47:41,530 --> 00:47:42,890
What do you want me to do?

1282
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:46,400
Leia, may I ask you
what you do for a living?

1283
00:47:46,400 --> 00:47:49,230
- Me?
- At first, I got a feeling...

1284
00:47:49,230 --> 00:47:50,470
that you were a journalist.

1285
00:47:50,470 --> 00:47:53,970
You have a very good deduction.

1286
00:47:53,970 --> 00:47:55,540
The occupation...

1287
00:47:55,540 --> 00:47:57,680
- It doesn't matter.
- doesn't really matter.

1288
00:47:57,680 --> 00:48:00,250
If it did, it'd be unfair for me.

1289
00:48:00,250 --> 00:48:01,750
- Right.
- Right.

1290
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:06,280
The special meal has arrived.

1291
00:48:06,650 --> 00:48:07,790
- Oh, chicken.
- Ta-da.

1292
00:48:08,650 --> 00:48:10,860
That's intense.

1293
00:48:10,860 --> 00:48:13,360
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

1294
00:48:13,360 --> 00:48:15,790
I feel rich to have chicken here.

1295
00:48:15,790 --> 00:48:16,800
Right.

1296
00:48:16,930 --> 00:48:17,930
Hey.

1297
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:24,870
The 3 of us had 2 meals...

1298
00:48:24,870 --> 00:48:26,640
for five diamonds.

1299
00:48:26,910 --> 00:48:28,840
That's 5,000 dollars,
and that's very expensive.

1300
00:48:28,840 --> 00:48:30,540
We decided to tighten our belts...

1301
00:48:30,540 --> 00:48:32,180
and find a way through.

1302
00:48:32,180 --> 00:48:34,150
That's what was on my mind.

1303
00:48:34,450 --> 00:48:35,650
It didn't make sense to me.

1304
00:48:35,650 --> 00:48:38,950
We're not here to have
chicken or pork belly.

1305
00:48:38,950 --> 00:48:40,850
We're not here to waste our money here.

1306
00:48:40,850 --> 00:48:43,220
We plan to secure
as much prize money as possible.

1307
00:48:43,560 --> 00:48:46,020
And we'll spend it...

1308
00:48:46,020 --> 00:48:48,130
on our play instead of food.

1309
00:48:48,130 --> 00:48:51,630
I don't think we'll be having
any luxurious meals until the end.

1310
00:48:56,570 --> 00:48:57,670
That scares me.

1311
00:48:58,500 --> 00:49:01,340
May I have your attention, please?

1312
00:49:01,540 --> 00:49:04,980
We will now play the Majority Rules Game.

1313
00:49:04,980 --> 00:49:08,450
The Majority Rules Game will be played
no more than six times.

1314
00:49:08,450 --> 00:49:12,080
Using the questions on values
from the pre-test,

1315
00:49:12,080 --> 00:49:13,920
the residents will speak...

1316
00:49:13,920 --> 00:49:17,290
their opinions freely.

1317
00:49:17,290 --> 00:49:19,790
Any resident who volunteers to speak...

1318
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:21,760
gets a banana as a prize.

1319
00:49:22,460 --> 00:49:24,160
After everyone finishes speaking,

1320
00:49:24,160 --> 00:49:28,770
residents will vote for
the approach that is likely...

1321
00:49:28,770 --> 00:49:30,640
to win more people's support.

1322
00:49:31,700 --> 00:49:32,900
After voting,

1323
00:49:32,900 --> 00:49:35,870
the person who successfully voted
for the one most people agreed with...

1324
00:49:35,870 --> 00:49:39,280
and matches majority's code...

1325
00:49:39,280 --> 00:49:40,680
gets two points.

1326
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:42,410
The person who successfully voted
for the one most people agreed with,

1327
00:49:42,410 --> 00:49:45,480
but doesn't match majority's code...

1328
00:49:45,480 --> 00:49:47,150
gets one point.

1329
00:49:47,520 --> 00:49:50,260
The pre-test had various questions.

1330
00:49:50,260 --> 00:49:52,520
Some questions might have...

1331
00:49:52,520 --> 00:49:55,090
a different code
from the way you answered.

1332
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:59,400
Regardless of the response,
the points are calculated...

1333
00:49:59,560 --> 00:50:03,100
based on the final code.

1334
00:50:03,570 --> 00:50:05,670
Therefore, if more people are...

1335
00:50:05,670 --> 00:50:09,710
expected to vote against your code,

1336
00:50:09,710 --> 00:50:11,280
you may vote for a different opinion...

1337
00:50:11,280 --> 00:50:13,950
or make a different statement...

1338
00:50:13,950 --> 00:50:16,180
to win points.

1339
00:50:16,780 --> 00:50:18,050
It's important to stir people...

1340
00:50:18,050 --> 00:50:19,580
for points, right?

1341
00:50:19,580 --> 00:50:20,590
You're right.

1342
00:50:20,750 --> 00:50:22,550
It's a matter of exposing my code...

1343
00:50:22,550 --> 00:50:24,860
to get more points...

1344
00:50:24,860 --> 00:50:27,030
or use a feint to protect my code,

1345
00:50:27,030 --> 00:50:29,130
but get a few points.

1346
00:50:29,130 --> 00:50:32,800
Also, a resident
with the most outstanding statement...

1347
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:34,600
will become an MVP in every game.

1348
00:50:34,600 --> 00:50:35,600
(An MVP will be selected
through voting at the end of every game.)

1349
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:37,670
The MVP will...

1350
00:50:37,670 --> 00:50:39,500
receive extra three points...

1351
00:50:39,500 --> 00:50:42,140
regardless of majority's opinion.

1352
00:50:42,710 --> 00:50:45,340
However, if two people receive
the same number of votes,

1353
00:50:45,340 --> 00:50:48,380
no MVP will be announced.

1354
00:50:49,280 --> 00:50:51,780
(They played the Majority Rules Game
in the evening of Day 1.)

1355
00:50:51,780 --> 00:50:53,650
(Self-driving cars should be designed
to save majority...)

1356
00:50:53,650 --> 00:50:55,590
(and sacrifice the driver
in case of a crash.)

1357
00:50:55,690 --> 00:50:58,420
It's important to follow the rule.

1358
00:50:58,420 --> 00:51:00,090
The moment you drive a self-driving car,

1359
00:51:00,090 --> 00:51:02,860
you're up alone against many,
so you'll die.

1360
00:51:02,860 --> 00:51:04,000
Would you drive it then?

1361
00:51:04,360 --> 00:51:05,360
Will self-driving car companies be able to
sell them?

1362
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:07,430
Everyone. Driving on your own is
the whole point of driving.

1363
00:51:07,430 --> 00:51:09,100
Don't drive a self-driving car.

1364
00:51:10,500 --> 00:51:12,100
Still, it's better to save many...

1365
00:51:12,100 --> 00:51:13,710
than just one.

1366
00:51:13,710 --> 00:51:14,970
If a sacrifice is necessary,

1367
00:51:14,970 --> 00:51:17,310
wouldn't it be better to sacrifice myself
than sacrificing many?

1368
00:51:17,310 --> 00:51:18,980
A sacrifice is wonderful,

1369
00:51:18,980 --> 00:51:20,050
but it's unreasonable...

1370
00:51:20,050 --> 00:51:23,350
to force you to sacrifice yourself...

1371
00:51:23,350 --> 00:51:24,620
the moment you get in the car.

1372
00:51:24,620 --> 00:51:26,680
I don't think it's unfair.

1373
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:27,990
Why is there no option?

1374
00:51:27,990 --> 00:51:29,450
Just drive another car.

1375
00:51:29,450 --> 00:51:32,090
You don't buy a self-driving car
to sacrifice yourself.

1376
00:51:32,090 --> 00:51:33,860
You buy it to make driving easy.

1377
00:51:33,860 --> 00:51:36,760
But if that condition is given,

1378
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:39,930
it's not like you have no other options
for cars.

1379
00:51:39,930 --> 00:51:42,070
According to the self-driving car data,

1380
00:51:42,070 --> 00:51:44,240
the chance of an accident is...

1381
00:51:44,240 --> 00:51:45,940
significantly lower...

1382
00:51:45,940 --> 00:51:48,040
when AI drives
than when the driver drives the car.

1383
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:49,510
For a motor company,

1384
00:51:49,510 --> 00:51:51,780
the accident handling cost is lower
when a few people die.

1385
00:51:51,780 --> 00:51:53,280
In terms of the cost...

1386
00:51:53,280 --> 00:51:54,280
That's crazy.

1387
00:51:54,510 --> 00:51:55,610
Think about it.

1388
00:51:55,610 --> 00:51:56,780
Make up your mind,

1389
00:51:56,780 --> 00:51:59,280
so we can share the points together.

1390
00:51:59,820 --> 00:52:00,820
Let's do this.

1391
00:52:02,450 --> 00:52:03,460
There's no time.

1392
00:52:03,460 --> 00:52:04,920
Let me make a quick statement.

1393
00:52:04,920 --> 00:52:06,060
(Majority Rules Game)

1394
00:52:06,060 --> 00:52:07,060
Hurry up.

1395
00:52:07,190 --> 00:52:08,190
Hurry up.

1396
00:52:08,930 --> 00:52:09,930
No.

1397
00:52:09,930 --> 00:52:11,000
(It was so intense, they ran out of time
on Day 1.)

1398
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:12,960
To prevent any accidents...

1399
00:52:12,960 --> 00:52:15,000
- caused by lack of driving skills...
- Time's up.

1400
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:17,300
That's a shame.

1401
00:52:17,670 --> 00:52:20,170
Six for principlism
and seven for consequentialism.

1402
00:52:20,170 --> 00:52:21,470
It's 6 to 7.

1403
00:52:21,470 --> 00:52:23,680
That was so close.
That's one vote difference.

1404
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:26,540
I supported principlism,

1405
00:52:26,540 --> 00:52:28,080
but I needed the point.

1406
00:52:28,080 --> 00:52:29,280
So I shifted to consequentialism.

1407
00:52:29,280 --> 00:52:31,450
I knew I'd still win a point.

1408
00:52:31,450 --> 00:52:33,080
I thought the majority would...

1409
00:52:33,080 --> 00:52:36,590
support consequentialism.

1410
00:52:36,790 --> 00:52:39,560
But I just didn't want to support it.

1411
00:52:39,560 --> 00:52:41,790
That was just wrong.

1412
00:52:42,130 --> 00:52:45,700
Even if that was the majority's opinion,

1413
00:52:45,930 --> 00:52:48,870
I just couldn't agree.

1414
00:52:49,530 --> 00:52:52,200
Today's MVP is Vector.

1415
00:52:53,770 --> 00:52:58,410
(Vector wins 3 extra points
for becoming an MVP.)

1416
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:02,780
Vector did make a good point,

1417
00:53:03,010 --> 00:53:05,250
and it'd be advantageous...

1418
00:53:05,250 --> 00:53:07,950
to make Vector an MVP...

1419
00:53:07,950 --> 00:53:10,460
since he doesn't belong to any team.

1420
00:53:11,790 --> 00:53:13,320
We don't know
what these points are for yet.

1421
00:53:13,320 --> 00:53:14,930
- Right.
- Right.

1422
00:53:14,930 --> 00:53:16,960
Anyway, it's going to be important...

1423
00:53:16,960 --> 00:53:19,130
as it goes. That's all we need to know.

1424
00:53:19,130 --> 00:53:21,130
There's nothing bad
about having many points.

1425
00:53:21,130 --> 00:53:23,370
The topic
for the Majority Rules Game is...

1426
00:53:23,800 --> 00:53:27,170
giving everyone a chance
to take the test...

1427
00:53:27,170 --> 00:53:31,840
creates a fair competition.

1428
00:53:31,840 --> 00:53:33,550
- Ability and structure?
- Fair competition.

1429
00:53:33,550 --> 00:53:35,310
- Oh, is that right?
- Ability and structure?

1430
00:53:35,310 --> 00:53:37,080
Structure and ability.

1431
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:39,220
A fair competition?

1432
00:53:39,220 --> 00:53:40,490
What is "fairness?"

1433
00:53:41,520 --> 00:53:43,590
They'll keep increasing the level
to more uncomfortable topics.

1434
00:53:44,360 --> 00:53:46,890
Things are definitely more sensitive
than yesterday.

1435
00:53:47,760 --> 00:53:49,430
For an hour starting now,

1436
00:53:49,960 --> 00:53:52,660
residents can freely share
their opinions...

1437
00:53:52,930 --> 00:53:55,430
on the podium set up in front.

1438
00:53:55,570 --> 00:53:56,770
I don't know what to say.

1439
00:53:59,970 --> 00:54:00,970
Which way do we go?

1440
00:54:01,840 --> 00:54:02,870
Which way...

1441
00:54:03,780 --> 00:54:05,340
I'm Team Ability.

1442
00:54:05,980 --> 00:54:06,980
Are you Team Ability?

1443
00:54:07,250 --> 00:54:08,250
Yes.

1444
00:54:09,550 --> 00:54:10,780
Are you Team Ability or Team Structure?

1445
00:54:10,920 --> 00:54:12,720
I'm not sure. I'm thinking about it.

1446
00:54:14,320 --> 00:54:17,020
For today's Majority Rules Game,

1447
00:54:17,620 --> 00:54:19,320
should I lie about my values?

1448
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:21,730
I spoke up so much yesterday,

1449
00:54:21,730 --> 00:54:23,700
so I thought it'd be very easy
for people to guess my code...

1450
00:54:23,700 --> 00:54:26,230
if I ended up revealing another one.

1451
00:54:26,760 --> 00:54:29,030
Because this is related
to our personal scores,

1452
00:54:29,030 --> 00:54:31,640
I thought higher scores would be
more convenient than lower scores.

1453
00:54:32,100 --> 00:54:34,370
So I realized that the strategy...

1454
00:54:34,510 --> 00:54:36,170
of totally hiding my code...

1455
00:54:36,170 --> 00:54:38,480
will make it difficult for me...

1456
00:54:38,480 --> 00:54:40,350
to earn personal points.

1457
00:54:40,350 --> 00:54:42,750
I felt this needed more thought
than expected.

1458
00:54:44,250 --> 00:54:46,950
"An equal opportunity to take the test..."

1459
00:54:48,150 --> 00:54:49,450
This is so hard.

1460
00:54:49,750 --> 00:54:50,760
I'll go.

1461
00:54:52,020 --> 00:54:56,230
(The first speaker
of the Majority Rules Game, Luna)

1462
00:54:57,160 --> 00:54:58,760
Normally, I would've been able...

1463
00:54:58,960 --> 00:55:02,230
to present more arguments
for the other side.

1464
00:55:02,500 --> 00:55:04,940
But since I was on the "Ability" side,

1465
00:55:04,940 --> 00:55:06,740
I thought I needed to push that more.

1466
00:55:06,740 --> 00:55:09,240
That's why I quickly thought
of my arguments.

1467
00:55:09,970 --> 00:55:13,540
Firstly, I believe that giving everyone
an equal opportunity to take the test...

1468
00:55:13,540 --> 00:55:17,450
is enough to satisfy
the conditions of fair competition.

1469
00:55:18,050 --> 00:55:20,450
Of course,
there are other necessary conditions.

1470
00:55:20,650 --> 00:55:23,020
For example, some people may not be
able to afford test preparation books.

1471
00:55:23,190 --> 00:55:25,860
Some people may not be
able to get good private education.

1472
00:55:25,860 --> 00:55:27,490
I can think of those conditions.

1473
00:55:27,660 --> 00:55:31,160
But because it's not possible
to add those conditions,

1474
00:55:31,160 --> 00:55:32,660
I think it's enough.

1475
00:55:32,830 --> 00:55:35,900
Let's say we add extra conditions.

1476
00:55:36,030 --> 00:55:38,500
That will cause
other points of unfairness.

1477
00:55:38,570 --> 00:55:42,070
In the end, we cannot create
what we call "fairness."

1478
00:55:42,170 --> 00:55:44,580
There will just be
new points of unfairness.

1479
00:55:44,610 --> 00:55:46,940
What I believe "enough" means here...

1480
00:55:47,180 --> 00:55:49,110
is letting people start...

1481
00:55:49,250 --> 00:55:52,580
at a reasonably similar starting line
within realistic conditions.

1482
00:55:52,850 --> 00:55:56,490
That's why I believe we can say
it's enough...

1483
00:55:56,490 --> 00:55:58,890
to give people the opportunity
to take the same test.

1484
00:55:59,520 --> 00:56:00,560
Thank you.

1485
00:56:00,560 --> 00:56:02,790
(Luna argued for "Ability"
in accordance with her code.)

1486
00:56:05,430 --> 00:56:06,900
I was planning to speak a bit later,

1487
00:56:07,070 --> 00:56:09,400
but I came to argue for the other side.

1488
00:56:10,030 --> 00:56:11,970
I go to schools...

1489
00:56:11,970 --> 00:56:14,210
to speak about sex education.

1490
00:56:14,470 --> 00:56:16,540
When you teach sex education in schools,

1491
00:56:16,540 --> 00:56:18,310
you run into very interesting situations.

1492
00:56:18,310 --> 00:56:21,010
There was an elderly person
at my lesson...

1493
00:56:21,010 --> 00:56:24,180
sitting next to a teenager.

1494
00:56:24,480 --> 00:56:26,650
I thought, "What's going on here?"

1495
00:56:26,780 --> 00:56:29,120
They were the child of immigrants.
That's quite common.

1496
00:56:29,320 --> 00:56:31,360
Children of immigrants...

1497
00:56:31,360 --> 00:56:33,660
aren't totally familiar with our language.

1498
00:56:33,760 --> 00:56:36,830
Us saying to those people,
"Hey, you are the one who chose Korea."

1499
00:56:36,830 --> 00:56:40,600
"Then you should put in the effort
and do the same as everyone else."

1500
00:56:40,670 --> 00:56:42,300
I believe that is too cruel...

1501
00:56:42,300 --> 00:56:44,870
and dismissive of those policies.

1502
00:56:44,870 --> 00:56:47,140
I actually studied abroad in the US.

1503
00:56:47,740 --> 00:56:50,880
Some could say I had a big disadvantage...

1504
00:56:51,440 --> 00:56:54,080
compared to local students
when I took the SATs.

1505
00:56:54,510 --> 00:56:57,320
Was I able to ask for more time...

1506
00:56:57,320 --> 00:56:59,880
because English wasn't my mother tongue?
Not at all.

1507
00:57:00,550 --> 00:57:04,160
If those who are taking...

1508
00:57:04,160 --> 00:57:07,090
the CSAT or SAT have the same goals,

1509
00:57:07,430 --> 00:57:09,990
I believe it's only fair
to take the test...

1510
00:57:10,090 --> 00:57:12,130
under the same conditions.

1511
00:57:14,730 --> 00:57:16,070
Does this need to be on the stand?

1512
00:57:16,530 --> 00:57:17,640
I can hold it, right?

1513
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:19,070
So cool.

1514
00:57:19,070 --> 00:57:22,470
Vector, who spoke just now,
had a disadvantage,

1515
00:57:22,470 --> 00:57:24,580
but won with his ability.

1516
00:57:24,640 --> 00:57:25,680
Congratulations.

1517
00:57:25,680 --> 00:57:28,480
- Thank you.
- I really admire you.

1518
00:57:28,650 --> 00:57:31,250
But on the other hand, I think about this.

1519
00:57:31,250 --> 00:57:32,550
Do you think the results...

1520
00:57:32,550 --> 00:57:35,050
we get are fair just because
we had the same opportunities?

1521
00:57:35,550 --> 00:57:38,120
Don't you think
that's a bit of an illusion?

1522
00:57:38,760 --> 00:57:40,560
Here's an example.

1523
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:42,660
A company is picking ten people
with an aptitude test,

1524
00:57:42,660 --> 00:57:45,100
and the top ten highest scorers
turn out to be all women.

1525
00:57:45,530 --> 00:57:48,400
In those situations, HR teams sometimes...

1526
00:57:48,530 --> 00:57:51,370
add a male candidate
who had a lower score.

1527
00:57:51,500 --> 00:57:54,910
I gave an example with one gender,
but the opposite happens as well.

1528
00:57:55,110 --> 00:57:56,840
When there are too many people...

1529
00:57:56,840 --> 00:58:00,040
of one category
when putting together a team,

1530
00:58:00,240 --> 00:58:03,780
companies take reactive measures
to compensate for it.

1531
00:58:03,980 --> 00:58:06,050
So I believe we need to let go...

1532
00:58:06,050 --> 00:58:08,590
of this fantasy we have about "fairness."

1533
00:58:08,950 --> 00:58:11,160
Also, thinking about the story
in this way...

1534
00:58:11,160 --> 00:58:12,890
will make it extra irritating.

1535
00:58:13,090 --> 00:58:14,490
Try putting yourself in that situation.

1536
00:58:14,590 --> 00:58:16,630
Imagine you're in that situation,

1537
00:58:16,630 --> 00:58:20,060
and someone else got in
because they got extra points.

1538
00:58:20,160 --> 00:58:23,230
That makes us feel
like something has been taken from us.

1539
00:58:23,400 --> 00:58:25,240
That makes it feel off-putting.

1540
00:58:25,370 --> 00:58:27,470
But you could create policies in this way.

1541
00:58:27,470 --> 00:58:29,170
Make the pie bigger.

1542
00:58:29,470 --> 00:58:31,340
From that perspective,

1543
00:58:31,340 --> 00:58:34,750
I believe we could at least improve...

1544
00:58:35,010 --> 00:58:38,220
those policies in a way that benefits...

1545
00:58:38,220 --> 00:58:39,480
the greater good of society.

1546
00:58:40,320 --> 00:58:42,350
I developed a crush.

1547
00:58:42,790 --> 00:58:45,120
She just speaks so well.

1548
00:58:46,560 --> 00:58:49,860
She criticized
what the previous speakers said...

1549
00:58:49,960 --> 00:58:51,730
while building her argument.

1550
00:58:52,130 --> 00:58:55,030
I really like people
who can speak like that.

1551
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,130
Out of the words written here,

1552
00:58:57,740 --> 00:58:59,740
I believe the word "fair..."

1553
00:58:59,740 --> 00:59:03,040
and the word "competition..."

1554
00:59:03,310 --> 00:59:05,580
don't really go well together.

1555
00:59:06,240 --> 00:59:10,210
Because when we get stuck
in the trap of wondering,

1556
00:59:10,310 --> 00:59:13,350
"What is the range of fairness
we need to consider..."

1557
00:59:13,350 --> 00:59:14,790
"for most people to think
something is fair,"

1558
00:59:14,990 --> 00:59:17,560
we end up thinking about it endlessly.

1559
00:59:17,860 --> 00:59:20,690
For example,
let's think about a track race.

1560
00:59:21,130 --> 00:59:23,690
If we can only say a race is fair...

1561
00:59:23,690 --> 00:59:25,030
if all runners have
the perfectly same physique,

1562
00:59:25,200 --> 00:59:27,500
the same leg length, for example,

1563
00:59:27,600 --> 00:59:29,270
the same amount of training,

1564
00:59:29,430 --> 00:59:30,800
the same condition on race day,

1565
00:59:30,800 --> 00:59:33,400
the same exact shoes,

1566
00:59:33,500 --> 00:59:35,340
and so on and so forth,

1567
00:59:35,540 --> 00:59:39,610
it'll feel too difficult
to meet those conditions at all.

1568
00:59:39,810 --> 00:59:43,480
That's why we aim for conditions
that can realistically be met.

1569
00:59:43,510 --> 00:59:47,790
By allowing everyone to take
the same test in the same amount of time,

1570
00:59:47,790 --> 00:59:51,320
we aim to at least make
the starting line the same for everyone.

1571
00:59:51,520 --> 00:59:53,720
It specifically says here, "enough."

1572
00:59:53,720 --> 00:59:55,860
(It's not enough, Structure, 2,
It's enough, Ability, 3)

1573
00:59:55,860 --> 00:59:58,860
I don't think "enough..."

1574
00:59:58,860 --> 01:00:02,370
and "at least" mean the same thing.

1575
01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:04,700
I think I would've agreed if this said,

1576
01:00:04,700 --> 01:00:06,340
"It satisfies the 'minimum' conditions."

1577
01:00:07,270 --> 01:00:10,010
I want to think a bit
about what sort of behavior...

1578
01:00:10,210 --> 01:00:12,980
the words "at least" and "enough..."

1579
01:00:12,980 --> 01:00:14,710
draw out of people.

1580
01:00:15,050 --> 01:00:18,750
When we believe something is enough,
we no longer act.

1581
01:00:19,050 --> 01:00:21,290
Something surprised me while being here.

1582
01:00:21,390 --> 01:00:24,460
Once my survival was guaranteed,

1583
01:00:24,690 --> 01:00:27,430
I can feel my body tighten up.

1584
01:00:27,690 --> 01:00:29,060
I become afraid to move.

1585
01:00:29,660 --> 01:00:32,630
I want you all to think
about how the word "enough..."

1586
01:00:32,630 --> 01:00:34,500
doesn't call us to action.

1587
01:00:34,500 --> 01:00:38,000
The meaning of the word "competition..."

1588
01:00:38,340 --> 01:00:40,070
is to rank people.

1589
01:00:40,340 --> 01:00:43,770
Even today, some of us will earn points,
and some of us won't.

1590
01:00:43,770 --> 01:00:47,080
I believe the results of competitions...

1591
01:00:47,080 --> 01:00:48,750
are inherently unfair.

1592
01:00:49,310 --> 01:00:51,250
The competition for a banana
is so intense.

1593
01:00:52,720 --> 01:00:54,720
"Enough," "overwhelmingly," "absolutely."

1594
01:00:54,720 --> 01:00:57,120
These sorts of sentences
are likely to be incorrect.

1595
01:00:57,120 --> 01:01:00,120
I was a bit surprised
that half of the people...

1596
01:01:00,120 --> 01:01:02,930
were arguing for "Ability,"
which is the opposite of that.

1597
01:01:03,130 --> 01:01:05,960
"Really? Are you sure?"

1598
01:01:06,300 --> 01:01:07,570
I'm still a bit surprised.

1599
01:01:07,570 --> 01:01:09,700
I guess that's how people think.

1600
01:01:10,030 --> 01:01:13,400
Listening to people
with different opinions than me...

1601
01:01:13,540 --> 01:01:14,670
is so fun.

1602
01:01:14,670 --> 01:01:18,480
Despite these differing opinions,
we're living together well in one land.

1603
01:01:19,140 --> 01:01:20,780
My daughter gifted me a poem,

1604
01:01:20,850 --> 01:01:23,510
and I particularly liked this one line.

1605
01:01:23,910 --> 01:01:26,280
"What roots does this tree have,"

1606
01:01:26,280 --> 01:01:28,520
"what trunk does this tree have,"

1607
01:01:29,290 --> 01:01:32,060
"that it was able to protect my yard
against these rough rainstorms?"

1608
01:01:32,420 --> 01:01:33,590
That was the line.

1609
01:01:34,590 --> 01:01:36,730
The roots of my parents,

1610
01:01:37,130 --> 01:01:40,530
as in, the environment they grew up in.

1611
01:01:40,700 --> 01:01:42,970
And the trunk, as in,
the efforts that they made.

1612
01:01:43,530 --> 01:01:45,800
"How did they become such good parents?"

1613
01:01:46,170 --> 01:01:48,810
That's the meaning the poem had for me.

1614
01:01:49,840 --> 01:01:53,280
For some trees,
the seeds fall on very good land.

1615
01:01:53,540 --> 01:01:55,310
Then they can really grow out their roots.

1616
01:01:55,910 --> 01:01:58,920
If so, they will be able to grow
strong trunks as well.

1617
01:01:58,920 --> 01:02:01,650
But some seeds fall in the desert.

1618
01:02:02,250 --> 01:02:04,720
If so, that person can work very hard...

1619
01:02:04,990 --> 01:02:06,260
but only grow thorns.

1620
01:02:07,290 --> 01:02:11,660
So I'm saying environment is important.

1621
01:02:11,960 --> 01:02:15,100
We all live together on one land.

1622
01:02:15,670 --> 01:02:19,840
Isn't it important for us to hold
that land together with our roots?

1623
01:02:20,300 --> 01:02:22,410
We need to prevent a landslide.

1624
01:02:22,410 --> 01:02:24,840
(It's not enough, Structure, 4,
It's enough, Ability, 4)

1625
01:02:25,640 --> 01:02:27,780
I had this thought.

1626
01:02:27,780 --> 01:02:29,080
He moved it out of the way.

1627
01:02:30,850 --> 01:02:33,480
Subsidies are nice.

1628
01:02:33,820 --> 01:02:34,890
Welfare is nice.

1629
01:02:34,990 --> 01:02:37,720
But I think sometimes,

1630
01:02:38,720 --> 01:02:41,360
that help takes away...

1631
01:02:41,890 --> 01:02:45,700
from one's will to take on a challenge.

1632
01:02:46,260 --> 01:02:48,030
I'll give you an example.

1633
01:02:48,300 --> 01:02:51,440
Let's say a rapper...

1634
01:02:51,440 --> 01:02:52,840
had a tough upbringing.

1635
01:02:52,840 --> 01:02:54,810
"I came from the ghetto."

1636
01:02:54,910 --> 01:02:56,970
"I got myself here
working at a pizza joint."

1637
01:02:56,970 --> 01:02:58,540
"I was mopping floors."

1638
01:02:58,540 --> 01:03:00,680
"Now, I'm wearing a Rolex."

1639
01:03:00,810 --> 01:03:02,210
"Do you see that? I did that."

1640
01:03:02,350 --> 01:03:05,420
But let's say the government
gives him a bunch of handouts...

1641
01:03:05,420 --> 01:03:06,750
to make things fair for him.

1642
01:03:06,880 --> 01:03:09,350
"I came here with disaster relief funds."

1643
01:03:09,420 --> 01:03:11,360
Doesn't that sound pretty uncool?

1644
01:03:11,360 --> 01:03:12,460
But won't you accept those funds?

1645
01:03:13,490 --> 01:03:15,290
I will. I appreciate them.

1646
01:03:15,460 --> 01:03:17,660
I want there to be more. But...

1647
01:03:18,330 --> 01:03:20,930
- I'm just presenting another side.
- Okay.

1648
01:03:21,530 --> 01:03:22,930
(He's so funny.)

1649
01:03:22,970 --> 01:03:25,100
Donkey was really shouting up there.

1650
01:03:25,200 --> 01:03:27,070
He was like an angry donkey on stage.

1651
01:03:27,270 --> 01:03:28,570
(Donkey, Stand-up comedian)

1652
01:03:28,570 --> 01:03:31,440
I thought I wanted to make
some sort of an impact,

1653
01:03:31,440 --> 01:03:33,810
even if that was by being ridiculous
and making people laugh.

1654
01:03:33,910 --> 01:03:36,080
We need fair opportunities,

1655
01:03:36,180 --> 01:03:39,320
not just for humanitarian reasons,
like to help a disadvantaged child...

1656
01:03:39,320 --> 01:03:41,450
make a better life for themselves,

1657
01:03:41,550 --> 01:03:44,190
but also to make our society wealthier.

1658
01:03:44,190 --> 01:03:46,790
I believe the total wealth
of our society increases...

1659
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:48,860
when a person with a good brain
is in a good position.

1660
01:03:49,030 --> 01:03:52,430
Let's say one person is born
into a rich family...

1661
01:03:52,430 --> 01:03:53,900
but isn't super smart,

1662
01:03:54,030 --> 01:03:56,330
and one person is very poor
but very smart.

1663
01:03:56,470 --> 01:03:59,000
If you ask which of these two
have the higher probability...

1664
01:03:59,000 --> 01:04:00,970
of getting into Seoul National University
in Korea's current society,

1665
01:04:01,040 --> 01:04:03,340
the person living in Gangnam...

1666
01:04:03,340 --> 01:04:06,480
is slightly more likely
to get into Seoul University.

1667
01:04:06,480 --> 01:04:10,280
Why? Because the opportunities
to study are already uneven.

1668
01:04:10,280 --> 01:04:11,950
And let's think,

1669
01:04:11,950 --> 01:04:14,450
"Who are the people taking tests?"

1670
01:04:14,550 --> 01:04:18,090
Most test takers are minors...

1671
01:04:18,090 --> 01:04:19,820
or people in their early 20s.

1672
01:04:19,960 --> 01:04:24,060
The life of a minor is shaped more...

1673
01:04:24,200 --> 01:04:26,430
by what is given to them
than by their own will.

1674
01:04:26,430 --> 01:04:28,430
Some kids get lucky with rich parents.

1675
01:04:28,430 --> 01:04:31,240
Or some kids won't be so lucky and end up
with parents who aren't as rich.

1676
01:04:31,240 --> 01:04:34,740
A society with disparities
in educational opportunities...

1677
01:04:34,740 --> 01:04:38,110
shouldn't be considered a fair society.
That's my opinion.

1678
01:04:38,110 --> 01:04:39,280
Some of you pointed out that...

1679
01:04:39,280 --> 01:04:42,310
smart people would more likely be accepted
into Seoul National University.

1680
01:04:42,580 --> 01:04:44,150
But being smart isn't everything.

1681
01:04:44,950 --> 01:04:46,950
Well, they might be more interested
in arts or sports.

1682
01:04:46,950 --> 01:04:48,650
Or they just might have poor character.

1683
01:04:48,650 --> 01:04:51,920
Then there's a high probability
of not getting into SNU.

1684
01:04:52,090 --> 01:04:55,190
I think those were limited examples.

1685
01:04:55,190 --> 01:04:57,600
You said that children
from wealthy backgrounds...

1686
01:04:57,600 --> 01:04:59,260
would have a higher likelihood...

1687
01:04:59,260 --> 01:05:00,530
of getting into Seoul National University.

1688
01:05:00,530 --> 01:05:02,500
I think
that's a huge generalization error.

1689
01:05:02,500 --> 01:05:05,000
I'd like to use my experience
when I was studying abroad as an example.

1690
01:05:05,000 --> 01:05:07,000
I met so many students who grew up
in much more supportive homes...

1691
01:05:07,000 --> 01:05:09,740
and had far better
educational opportunities.

1692
01:05:09,940 --> 01:05:12,580
I worked really hard to beat them.

1693
01:05:12,740 --> 01:05:14,880
In the end,
I got into a more prestigious university.

1694
01:05:15,010 --> 01:05:17,450
Now that my annual income is higher
than theirs...

1695
01:05:17,620 --> 01:05:19,380
and I'm earning more than them,

1696
01:05:19,380 --> 01:05:22,050
the feeling of accomplishment
is far greater than theirs.

1697
01:05:22,250 --> 01:05:25,860
Political correctness is widespread
in the US.

1698
01:05:25,860 --> 01:05:29,660
Sometimes, schools give extra points
to Black students.

1699
01:05:29,660 --> 01:05:31,030
So if two students had identical grades,

1700
01:05:31,030 --> 01:05:34,630
a Black applicant might get accepted
while a White applicant wouldn't.

1701
01:05:34,800 --> 01:05:37,940
If you think about it,
this student was discriminated...

1702
01:05:38,070 --> 01:05:39,970
based on the color of their skin.

1703
01:05:39,970 --> 01:05:42,010
Structural interventions...

1704
01:05:42,010 --> 01:05:45,780
might just end up causing conflicts
within the society.

1705
01:05:45,940 --> 01:05:47,950
Well, she mentioned the racial issue.

1706
01:05:48,110 --> 01:05:50,580
Bringing up racial discrimination
or reverse discrimination was iffy.

1707
01:05:50,580 --> 01:05:53,120
All the speakers here
are neither Black nor White.

1708
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:55,820
Is it something we can bring up
on behalf of other people?

1709
01:05:55,820 --> 01:05:57,290
I was a bit concerned.

1710
01:05:57,660 --> 01:05:59,460
People are concerned
about these structural changes...

1711
01:05:59,460 --> 01:06:01,230
such as reverse discrimination.

1712
01:06:01,390 --> 01:06:02,560
If the changes are too much,

1713
01:06:02,560 --> 01:06:04,190
people will criticize them
and they will eventually disappear.

1714
01:06:04,190 --> 01:06:05,360
The market economy...

1715
01:06:05,360 --> 01:06:07,560
isn't the only place
the Invisible Hand exists.

1716
01:06:07,560 --> 01:06:10,170
I believe we naturally find the balance...

1717
01:06:10,170 --> 01:06:12,500
in social agreements.

1718
01:06:12,500 --> 01:06:17,710
With that said,
I don't think that argument fits here.

1719
01:06:18,210 --> 01:06:20,110
(The speaking time is over.)

1720
01:06:20,110 --> 01:06:22,080
The speaking time has ended.

1721
01:06:23,280 --> 01:06:26,580
You will now vote
for the Majority Rules Game.

1722
01:06:27,280 --> 01:06:31,390
Residents, vote for the side
you believe will be the majority.

1723
01:06:31,620 --> 01:06:33,560
Write down your pick for MVP.

1724
01:06:33,560 --> 01:06:35,090
- And drop it in the ballot box.
- My gosh.

1725
01:06:35,090 --> 01:06:36,360
This is tough.

1726
01:06:36,360 --> 01:06:38,560
Once all votes are in,

1727
01:06:39,130 --> 01:06:42,000
today's majority side and MVP
will be revealed.

1728
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:44,570
Why didn't you speak today, Boss?

1729
01:06:44,570 --> 01:06:46,100
- Me?
- I was curious about your opinion.

1730
01:06:46,100 --> 01:06:47,740
- I agree with the statement.
- Okay.

1731
01:06:47,740 --> 01:06:50,980
But my experience
is mostly military-related.

1732
01:06:51,080 --> 01:06:52,510
So it might be uncomfortable.

1733
01:06:52,510 --> 01:06:54,480
I might have found it uncomfortable
discussing it.

1734
01:06:54,480 --> 01:06:57,010
So let me use the physical fitness
as an example.

1735
01:06:57,210 --> 01:06:58,380
When female soldiers
have to do 50 repetitions,

1736
01:06:58,380 --> 01:07:00,080
male soldiers have to do 80 repetitions.

1737
01:07:00,080 --> 01:07:01,320
Some said that it wasn't fair.

1738
01:07:01,820 --> 01:07:04,920
"Bullets don't steer clear of someone
just because they are women."

1739
01:07:04,920 --> 01:07:06,220
I've heard a lot of people say that.

1740
01:07:06,220 --> 01:07:07,320
But I think it's fair...

1741
01:07:07,320 --> 01:07:09,430
because men and women differ
in physical strength...

1742
01:07:09,430 --> 01:07:10,660
and muscular power.

1743
01:07:10,860 --> 01:07:12,760
But I thought I would be uncomfortable
discussing that.

1744
01:07:12,760 --> 01:07:14,430
- So you were being careful.
- So I decided not to speak up.

1745
01:07:14,430 --> 01:07:17,570
Today, our debate was neck and neck.

1746
01:07:17,570 --> 01:07:19,670
Everyone came up to speak today.

1747
01:07:19,670 --> 01:07:20,740
Yes, totally.

1748
01:07:20,740 --> 01:07:22,910
Wasn't it really interesting?

1749
01:07:23,440 --> 01:07:25,210
- You got those crazy eyes.
- Why are you so excited?

1750
01:07:25,540 --> 01:07:28,480
She loves a dopamine rush.
She can't say no to it.

1751
01:07:31,180 --> 01:07:32,850
The results of the Majority Rules Game...

1752
01:07:32,850 --> 01:07:34,720
- will be announced now.
- Drumroll, please.

1753
01:07:34,920 --> 01:07:37,290
- Drumroll, please.
- Today's theme was...

1754
01:07:37,420 --> 01:07:40,520
"Giving everyone an equal opportunity
to take the test..."

1755
01:07:40,520 --> 01:07:44,930
"is enough to satisfy the conditions
of fair competition."

1756
01:07:45,060 --> 01:07:46,830
- Here are the results.
- Let's see.

1757
01:07:46,830 --> 01:07:47,830
I'm nervous.

1758
01:07:47,830 --> 01:07:49,970
Three votes for Structure.
Ten votes for Ability.

1759
01:07:50,370 --> 01:07:53,570
Today's majority side
has leaned toward Ability.

1760
01:07:54,540 --> 01:07:55,610
- No way.
- Ten to three?

1761
01:07:55,610 --> 01:07:57,010
- They all switched.
- No way.

1762
01:07:57,010 --> 01:07:58,980
- They all switched.
- They switched.

1763
01:07:58,980 --> 01:08:00,940
People who leaned
toward Structure initially...

1764
01:08:01,050 --> 01:08:02,110
- That's interesting.
- I'm sorry.

1765
01:08:02,110 --> 01:08:03,580
- That's right.
- Here's an honest statement.

1766
01:08:03,980 --> 01:08:05,480
- Did you vote for Ability?
- Yes.

1767
01:08:06,250 --> 01:08:07,250
- I was desperate.
- Really?

1768
01:08:07,250 --> 01:08:09,050
I still don't agree
with ability-based policies.

1769
01:08:09,350 --> 01:08:10,820
I lean heavily toward Structure.

1770
01:08:10,820 --> 01:08:14,760
I still believe structure and policies
play a crucial role in our society.

1771
01:08:14,760 --> 01:08:16,160
But this is the Majority Rules Game.

1772
01:08:16,160 --> 01:08:17,560
After listening to everyone,

1773
01:08:17,560 --> 01:08:19,360
I counted the votes.

1774
01:08:19,700 --> 01:08:21,330
It seemed they were the majority,
so I voted for that.

1775
01:08:21,570 --> 01:08:23,900
I noticed something about the residents
arguing for Ability.

1776
01:08:24,100 --> 01:08:26,540
It looked like
they weren't going to change their vote.

1777
01:08:26,700 --> 01:08:28,540
I thought people
who leaned toward Structure...

1778
01:08:28,540 --> 01:08:30,170
might change their vote.

1779
01:08:30,170 --> 01:08:32,280
Deep down, I still lean toward Structure.

1780
01:08:32,510 --> 01:08:34,810
But I voted for Ability
and got on the majority side.

1781
01:08:34,950 --> 01:08:37,480
First of all,
even if it didn't agree with my belief,

1782
01:08:37,580 --> 01:08:39,550
I was going to side with the majority
no matter what.

1783
01:08:39,850 --> 01:08:41,190
(Structure: Leia, Salt, Hamlet)

1784
01:08:41,190 --> 01:08:45,120
(Ability: Luna, Paul, Maillard, Donkey,
Vector, Boss, Genie, Siseon, Izaha, Pitou)

1785
01:08:45,190 --> 01:08:47,160
- I thought I wouldn't change my vote.
- This is crazy.

1786
01:08:47,160 --> 01:08:49,230
- Points were at stake.
- Of course.

1787
01:08:49,230 --> 01:08:50,760
- You can't help it.
- I changed toward the end.

1788
01:08:53,430 --> 01:08:57,500
Leia and Izaha received the most votes
for today's MVP.

1789
01:08:57,670 --> 01:08:58,840
- As it's a tie,
- Two people?

1790
01:08:58,840 --> 01:09:00,270
- no one is MVP.
- It's invalid.

1791
01:09:00,370 --> 01:09:02,310
(There's no MVP today
because the vote ended in a tie.)

1792
01:09:02,310 --> 01:09:04,370
- The vote is void.
- What? No!

1793
01:09:04,580 --> 01:09:05,980
- My goodness.
- What?

1794
01:09:06,140 --> 01:09:07,610
- What? It's a tie?
- No.

1795
01:09:07,810 --> 01:09:09,450
- That's not good.
- Really?

1796
01:09:09,880 --> 01:09:11,120
It's not good.

1797
01:09:11,250 --> 01:09:12,320
That's zero points.

1798
01:09:13,950 --> 01:09:16,420
Today, I voted for Leia.

1799
01:09:16,690 --> 01:09:18,090
But the vote ended in a tie.

1800
01:09:18,260 --> 01:09:19,790
The vote was void.

1801
01:09:19,790 --> 01:09:23,960
So I thought, "Had I not voted for Leia,"

1802
01:09:23,960 --> 01:09:25,430
"Izaha would've gotten it."

1803
01:09:25,430 --> 01:09:27,060
I voted for Izaha.

1804
01:09:27,260 --> 01:09:30,530
Of course, I vote for the resident
who gets close to convincing me.

1805
01:09:30,670 --> 01:09:33,270
But I also vote for the resident
who does well in the debate.

1806
01:09:33,340 --> 01:09:34,970
Should I say he had a nice flow?

1807
01:09:34,970 --> 01:09:36,370
So I voted for him as the MVP.

1808
01:09:36,370 --> 01:09:40,540
To be honest, I wanted to be the MVP...

1809
01:09:40,540 --> 01:09:43,880
because once you're chosen as the MVP,
you get three points.

1810
01:09:44,080 --> 01:09:46,420
I didn't even vote for myself
when I ran for class president...

1811
01:09:46,420 --> 01:09:48,050
in elementary school.

1812
01:09:48,050 --> 01:09:49,690
(Leia, Journalist)

1813
01:09:49,690 --> 01:09:51,690
I voted for myself for the first time.

1814
01:09:52,460 --> 01:09:54,560
I didn't expect much.

1815
01:09:54,560 --> 01:09:58,560
But they paid attention to what I said
and could relate to it.

1816
01:09:58,560 --> 01:10:00,430
So I was grateful and had fun.

1817
01:10:00,760 --> 01:10:01,870
- Great job, everyone.
- But...

1818
01:10:01,870 --> 01:10:02,870
- Can't they both get three points?
- Great job.

1819
01:10:02,870 --> 01:10:04,100
- Congratulations.
- Well done.

1820
01:10:04,270 --> 01:10:05,400
What a bummer.

1821
01:10:05,840 --> 01:10:07,070
- My gosh.
- This is tough.

1822
01:10:07,070 --> 01:10:08,470
They should both get three points.

1823
01:10:08,470 --> 01:10:10,570
(MVP: Void)

1824
01:10:10,640 --> 01:10:13,510
The leaders will have a negotiation
in 30 minutes.

1825
01:10:13,510 --> 01:10:15,510
- A negotiation?
- When the negotiation time is called,

1826
01:10:15,810 --> 01:10:17,280
leaders of each team...

1827
01:10:17,280 --> 01:10:19,980
- must gather in the Community Center.
- What?

1828
01:10:19,980 --> 01:10:21,420
- Leaders will have a negotiation?
- What?

1829
01:10:22,950 --> 01:10:24,150
I guess the three leaders...

1830
01:10:24,150 --> 01:10:25,490
- will talk.
- I guess something's up.

1831
01:10:25,490 --> 01:10:26,660
- Something's up.
- Something's up.

1832
01:10:26,660 --> 01:10:28,360
- They didn't do this last night.
- Right. I guess so.

1833
01:10:28,360 --> 01:10:30,390
- Let's hurry up and go back.
- Okay. Let's go.

1834
01:10:30,390 --> 01:10:31,500
Let's hurry.

1835
01:10:31,560 --> 01:10:34,100
- Thirty minutes.
- What can the leaders discuss?

1836
01:10:34,100 --> 01:10:35,700
- Exactly.
- The negotiation...

1837
01:10:35,700 --> 01:10:37,770
I bet it has to do with a policy.

1838
01:10:37,770 --> 01:10:40,170
- They said they'd reveal it shortly.
- Yes.

1839
01:10:40,640 --> 01:10:42,340
I'll brief you guys once I come back.

1840
01:10:42,670 --> 01:10:43,670
Okay.

1841
01:10:43,670 --> 01:10:45,680
Hold on. What do you think...

1842
01:10:46,440 --> 01:10:47,910
we'll discuss?

1843
01:10:48,410 --> 01:10:50,380
I should take my notebook, right?

1844
01:10:50,380 --> 01:10:53,180
- Yes. Take notes on everything.
- Yes. You should.

1845
01:10:53,180 --> 01:10:55,050
- And share them with us.
- Yes. Right.

1846
01:10:55,050 --> 01:10:57,720
I don't know
what exactly we'll be discussing.

1847
01:10:57,720 --> 01:10:58,720
Right, we don't know.

1848
01:10:58,720 --> 01:11:00,090
- This is such an important assignment.
- Right. Even if...

1849
01:11:00,090 --> 01:11:02,090
We have no idea what it is.

1850
01:11:02,790 --> 01:11:07,000
(On the other hand, Vector is at ease
since it's just him in the team.)

1851
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:15,370
Leaders will have a negotiation soon.

1852
01:11:15,610 --> 01:11:18,580
The negotiation will be held every day
starting today.

1853
01:11:19,180 --> 01:11:22,150
The decisions made
during this negotiation...

1854
01:11:22,150 --> 01:11:24,680
can affect each team's resources
and conditions.

1855
01:11:24,850 --> 01:11:26,020
- It could affect the resources.
- I see.

1856
01:11:26,020 --> 01:11:27,880
- It could affect our team?
- I wonder what it is.

1857
01:11:28,250 --> 01:11:29,920
Once the negotiation ends,

1858
01:11:30,090 --> 01:11:33,020
today's life submission
will take place next.

1859
01:11:33,020 --> 01:11:34,830
- Take the lives with you.
- I see.

1860
01:11:35,690 --> 01:11:36,890
I totally forgot about that.

1861
01:11:37,060 --> 01:11:40,000
Leaders, bring the lives
you will submit today...

1862
01:11:40,400 --> 01:11:42,500
and resources you may use
during the negotiation...

1863
01:11:42,730 --> 01:11:45,000
- Resources...
- to the Community Center.

1864
01:11:45,000 --> 01:11:46,400
- Resources to use during the negotiation?
- Resources to use during the negotiation?

1865
01:11:46,700 --> 01:11:49,070
- What does that mean?
- You should take some credits with you.

1866
01:11:49,070 --> 01:11:50,970
- What? We have to use more of them?
- What? My gosh.

1867
01:11:51,110 --> 01:11:52,710
I don't want to use our credits.

1868
01:11:53,140 --> 01:11:55,510
I'll just bring the entire box.

1869
01:11:55,510 --> 01:11:56,510
- Okay.
- Yes.

1870
01:11:56,510 --> 01:11:58,980
It might be better
to keep them in the dark about...

1871
01:11:58,980 --> 01:12:00,580
- how many lives we have.
- Yes.

1872
01:12:00,580 --> 01:12:02,650
- We must trust you. That's the only way.
- Right.

1873
01:12:02,650 --> 01:12:04,250
- We have to give her the key.
- We trust you.

1874
01:12:04,250 --> 01:12:06,490
- Don't worry. And crush them.
- I got this. I'll be back.

1875
01:12:06,620 --> 01:12:08,160
- Good luck.
- As for this moment,

1876
01:12:08,160 --> 01:12:09,560
pursue Practicality.

1877
01:12:09,830 --> 01:12:11,030
- I always do.
- She always pursues Practicality.

1878
01:12:11,030 --> 01:12:12,900
- Then pursue it even more.
- Yes.

1879
01:12:22,210 --> 01:12:25,040
They're our lives.
You can't negotiate with them.

1880
01:12:25,810 --> 01:12:26,810
Of course, I won't.

1881
01:12:27,240 --> 01:12:28,780
- Of course, I won't.
- You'll have to come back then.

1882
01:12:28,780 --> 01:12:29,850
Of course, I won't.

1883
01:12:30,280 --> 01:12:31,850
These are our precious lives.

1884
01:12:31,850 --> 01:12:34,420
We went through so much trouble
to earn these lives.

1885
01:12:36,590 --> 01:12:37,750
- To the Community Center?
- Yes.

1886
01:12:38,360 --> 01:12:39,890
- Did you pack them?
- Yes, I did.

1887
01:12:39,890 --> 01:12:40,920
He packed enough.

1888
01:12:41,120 --> 01:12:42,460
I can't just take one.

1889
01:12:44,230 --> 01:12:46,500
- What? You only packed one life?
- My gosh.

1890
01:12:46,560 --> 01:12:47,660
What are you doing?

1891
01:12:47,860 --> 01:12:50,170
We're watching you.

1892
01:12:51,230 --> 01:12:52,300
Don't be silly.

1893
01:12:52,400 --> 01:12:53,570
- How...
- You're flustered.

1894
01:12:53,570 --> 01:12:56,070
You're trying to send us home
with that nice smile.

1895
01:12:56,210 --> 01:12:58,080
- My gosh.
- So you can be here for a week.

1896
01:13:00,180 --> 01:13:01,310
- Gosh, that's funny.
- What are you talking about?

1897
01:13:02,250 --> 01:13:03,410
Are you leaving now?

1898
01:13:03,410 --> 01:13:04,480
- Yes. They called the leaders now.
- They told me to come now.

1899
01:13:04,480 --> 01:13:05,980
- Okay. See you.
- Good luck.

1900
01:13:12,420 --> 01:13:13,560
You're waiting out here.

1901
01:13:13,990 --> 01:13:15,130
They told us to bring our resources.

1902
01:13:15,130 --> 01:13:16,830
Right.
They said we'd need them to negotiate.

1903
01:13:17,130 --> 01:13:18,230
You're going to join us?

1904
01:13:18,230 --> 01:13:19,400
- Yes. He's also a leader.
- I'm a leader too.

1905
01:13:19,560 --> 01:13:21,260
I'm a leader too.

1906
01:13:21,260 --> 01:13:22,470
(The isolation
of a one-person team leader)

1907
01:13:22,630 --> 01:13:24,430
- I'm a leader too.
- You're okay, right?

1908
01:13:24,770 --> 01:13:26,770
I had to use the bathroom. Sorry I'm late.

1909
01:13:26,970 --> 01:13:28,140
- Let's go in.
- Okay.

1910
01:13:28,570 --> 01:13:30,470
Why did they ask us
to bring our resources?

1911
01:13:31,610 --> 01:13:33,010
Leaders,

1912
01:13:33,010 --> 01:13:35,550
stand at your designated spot.

1913
01:13:36,150 --> 01:13:37,780
I think we have to stand over the light.

1914
01:13:37,780 --> 01:13:39,250
- This is black, right?
- Right there.

1915
01:13:39,250 --> 01:13:40,280
That's black.

1916
01:13:41,280 --> 01:13:42,850
- It's a black light.
- Yes.

1917
01:13:44,650 --> 01:13:49,660
(Leader Negotiation)

1918
01:13:50,560 --> 01:13:52,400
Welcome...

1919
01:13:52,400 --> 01:13:54,530
to the Leader Negotiation.

1920
01:13:54,800 --> 01:13:58,370
Today's Leader Negotiation will begin now.

1921
01:13:58,370 --> 01:14:00,340
At the first Leader Negotiation,

1922
01:14:00,340 --> 01:14:01,440
I was like, "What's this?"

1923
01:14:01,440 --> 01:14:03,910
The announcement said
we had to bring our resources.

1924
01:14:04,310 --> 01:14:06,380
I wondered if we would be able
to help each other...

1925
01:14:06,480 --> 01:14:08,080
or trade with other leaders.

1926
01:14:08,210 --> 01:14:09,950
During trading, we assumed that...

1927
01:14:09,950 --> 01:14:12,280
we could only trade
using our assigned resources.

1928
01:14:12,350 --> 01:14:15,290
But I thought we'd be able to trade
with other resources.

1929
01:14:15,390 --> 01:14:18,090
I thought it would be fun.

1930
01:14:18,090 --> 01:14:20,660
Perhaps, I can anticipate a twist.

1931
01:14:20,660 --> 01:14:22,260
Or it might change their opinions a bit.

1932
01:14:22,390 --> 01:14:24,730
I was super nervous
and didn't know what to do...

1933
01:14:24,730 --> 01:14:26,360
when I attended the negotiation.

1934
01:14:26,360 --> 01:14:28,370
"Leaders must fulfill
their convictions..."

1935
01:14:28,430 --> 01:14:31,000
"while bearing the responsibility
if things go wrong."

1936
01:14:31,000 --> 01:14:34,970
I've always thought
that was the requirement of a true leader.

1937
01:14:35,110 --> 01:14:36,810
To expand more on this idea,

1938
01:14:37,110 --> 01:14:40,540
I want leaders to contribute
to the community.

1939
01:14:40,880 --> 01:14:43,250
I'm hoping
the other leaders have a similar view.

1940
01:14:43,680 --> 01:14:46,750
First, the current pollution index
for the entire Community Town...

1941
01:14:46,750 --> 01:14:49,020
will be revealed.

1942
01:14:49,290 --> 01:14:51,490
The current pollution index...

1943
01:14:51,690 --> 01:14:53,690
- is at 15.
- Pollution?

1944
01:14:54,060 --> 01:14:55,790
Once the pollution index reaches 100,

1945
01:14:55,790 --> 01:14:57,530
the Community enters
a state of saturation.

1946
01:14:57,860 --> 01:14:59,430
Please pay attention to the index.

1947
01:14:59,960 --> 01:15:01,160
- The pollution index is at 15.
- The next item on the agenda...

1948
01:15:01,160 --> 01:15:03,200
will be announced shortly.

1949
01:15:03,200 --> 01:15:04,270
The pollution index?

1950
01:15:06,700 --> 01:15:08,040
The pollution index.

1951
01:15:08,410 --> 01:15:10,540
It's finally revealed. That's good.

1952
01:15:10,940 --> 01:15:13,980
There was an announcement
about the pollution index.

1953
01:15:13,980 --> 01:15:15,580
I was relieved.

1954
01:15:15,580 --> 01:15:17,010
Without that announcement,

1955
01:15:17,010 --> 01:15:19,350
it would've been very difficult for us...

1956
01:15:19,350 --> 01:15:21,620
to bring up pollution-free credits.

1957
01:15:21,720 --> 01:15:23,220
Yes. As you can see,

1958
01:15:23,220 --> 01:15:25,490
- it's marked in red.
- Yes.

1959
01:15:25,560 --> 01:15:27,290
I should give you an explanation.

1960
01:15:27,890 --> 01:15:29,130
- I see.
- The credits from earlier...

1961
01:15:29,830 --> 01:15:31,960
We got a new type of credit.
It's called a pollution-free credit.

1962
01:15:32,000 --> 01:15:34,660
We've been using pollution credits.

1963
01:15:35,100 --> 01:15:37,230
Every time we use it, it causes pollution.

1964
01:15:37,830 --> 01:15:39,270
The pollution index goes up.

1965
01:15:39,500 --> 01:15:40,900
- Then...
- Gosh.

1966
01:15:40,900 --> 01:15:43,710
we used a total of 15 credits so far.

1967
01:15:43,770 --> 01:15:46,240
I think it's at 15
because we used 15 credits in total.

1968
01:15:46,240 --> 01:15:49,310
- Vector didn't use any credits.
- I used zero credits.

1969
01:15:49,310 --> 01:15:51,580
Counting the number of trades
from Days 1 and 2,

1970
01:15:51,580 --> 01:15:53,350
- we would've used 6, 3 credits each day.
- Yes.

1971
01:15:53,350 --> 01:15:55,920
Each team used one credit...

1972
01:15:55,920 --> 01:15:57,750
- for the quiz today.
- Okay.

1973
01:15:57,750 --> 01:15:59,460
Let's say we used some credits for hints.

1974
01:15:59,460 --> 01:16:02,260
So the pollution index matches
the total number of credits...

1975
01:16:02,260 --> 01:16:04,230
used so far.

1976
01:16:04,660 --> 01:16:06,230
Anyway, it's at 15 now.

1977
01:16:06,700 --> 01:16:07,830
Once we hit 100,

1978
01:16:07,830 --> 01:16:10,070
- the skull will be colored in red.
- Yes.

1979
01:16:10,070 --> 01:16:11,970
- Yes.
- What we heard was quite terrifying.

1980
01:16:12,240 --> 01:16:13,640
Once it reaches 100,

1981
01:16:13,970 --> 01:16:17,270
there will be massive damage...

1982
01:16:17,440 --> 01:16:19,480
to everyone's assets
in the Community Town.

1983
01:16:19,810 --> 01:16:20,940
Damage to our assets?

1984
01:16:20,940 --> 01:16:22,550
We were told that it could incur losses...

1985
01:16:22,550 --> 01:16:24,980
- on everyone's assets.
- Oh, my gosh.

1986
01:16:25,520 --> 01:16:27,320
(During the resource collection)

1987
01:16:27,380 --> 01:16:30,850
It could result in critical damage...

1988
01:16:31,050 --> 01:16:33,960
to the safety and assets of everyone
in the Community Town.

1989
01:16:35,260 --> 01:16:38,060
That's why
when we were doing our mission today,

1990
01:16:38,460 --> 01:16:41,900
we were able to change our credits
to pollution-free credits.

1991
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:43,300
When you did,

1992
01:16:43,300 --> 01:16:44,470
how was the ratio?

1993
01:16:44,470 --> 01:16:45,570
It was half.

1994
01:16:46,740 --> 01:16:48,910
So our credit production...

1995
01:16:49,010 --> 01:16:51,140
will go down by half from here on out.

1996
01:16:52,110 --> 01:16:58,820
(Regular credits: 3)

1997
01:16:58,820 --> 01:17:02,050
(Pollution-free credit: 2)

1998
01:17:02,490 --> 01:17:05,560
(Maillard lowered the yield ratio
than the actual yield ratio.)

1999
01:17:06,060 --> 01:17:08,890
We heard that this pollution index...

2000
01:17:08,890 --> 01:17:10,930
would affect everyone's assets.

2001
01:17:10,930 --> 01:17:13,760
With the intention to prevent
as much pollution as possible,

2002
01:17:13,760 --> 01:17:15,830
we chose pollution-free credits.

2003
01:17:15,830 --> 01:17:18,100
If we choose pollution-free credits,

2004
01:17:18,130 --> 01:17:19,270
as you know,

2005
01:17:19,270 --> 01:17:22,040
the number of credits for all of us
would decrease.

2006
01:17:23,270 --> 01:17:26,540
Our opportunities
for productive activities would go down.

2007
01:17:29,250 --> 01:17:30,510
Then...

2008
01:17:30,510 --> 01:17:32,020
we should discuss whether or not...

2009
01:17:32,020 --> 01:17:33,350
we should get more pollution credits...

2010
01:17:33,350 --> 01:17:35,720
while keeping the number under 100
although it might be risky.

2011
01:17:35,720 --> 01:17:37,720
Or we should just go
with only pollution-free credits.

2012
01:17:37,720 --> 01:17:39,620
- We should...
- Here's the problem.

2013
01:17:39,620 --> 01:17:41,490
We don't have that many credits.

2014
01:17:41,490 --> 01:17:43,590
But we might not be able to
produce more credits tomorrow.

2015
01:17:43,590 --> 01:17:47,600
Here's the thing.
We didn't get to buy enough lives today.

2016
01:17:47,800 --> 01:17:50,330
It looks like all three teams...

2017
01:17:50,330 --> 01:17:51,500
will...

2018
01:17:51,700 --> 01:17:53,470
try to earn more lives tomorrow.

2019
01:17:53,470 --> 01:17:56,040
That means
there won't be any credits tomorrow.

2020
01:17:57,740 --> 01:18:00,180
Then we'll have a limited number
of credits the day after tomorrow.

2021
01:18:00,180 --> 01:18:01,850
And we'll still be short on lives again.

2022
01:18:01,850 --> 01:18:03,880
Yes. So this is...

2023
01:18:03,950 --> 01:18:05,480
a vicious cycle on repeat.

2024
01:18:07,750 --> 01:18:09,690
So that sums up our situation.

2025
01:18:10,120 --> 01:18:12,890
Maybe, this is like a test.

2026
01:18:12,890 --> 01:18:14,990
We can get more regular credits...

2027
01:18:14,990 --> 01:18:18,190
and use them until the index reaches 100.

2028
01:18:18,190 --> 01:18:20,030
I mean, we can do that.

2029
01:18:20,300 --> 01:18:23,030
For communal interests,

2030
01:18:23,030 --> 01:18:25,200
we have to be less selfish.

2031
01:18:25,200 --> 01:18:29,410
Will we be able to keep the index
below the threshold?

2032
01:18:29,410 --> 01:18:30,770
With this announcement,

2033
01:18:30,770 --> 01:18:32,710
there are more things my team can do now.

2034
01:18:32,810 --> 01:18:34,640
My team can use...

2035
01:18:34,640 --> 01:18:37,110
regular credits,
and we can use a lot of them...

2036
01:18:37,110 --> 01:18:40,150
while selling pollution-free credits.

2037
01:18:40,380 --> 01:18:43,990
I wanted to use the new system
with pollution-free credits.

2038
01:18:43,990 --> 01:18:45,790
The leaders at today's negotiation...

2039
01:18:45,790 --> 01:18:47,990
were quite innocent.

2040
01:18:47,990 --> 01:18:48,990
They believed me.

2041
01:18:48,990 --> 01:18:51,930
I exaggerated a bit to scare them.

2042
01:18:51,930 --> 01:18:54,730
They took everything I said at face value.

2043
01:18:55,530 --> 01:18:56,700
I thought, "This is nice."

2044
01:18:57,270 --> 01:18:59,200
- Until tomorrow...
- Then the pollution index...

2045
01:18:59,200 --> 01:19:01,240
Let's say
there's another negotiation tomorrow...

2046
01:19:01,240 --> 01:19:03,170
- and we discuss the pollution index.
- Okay.

2047
01:19:03,170 --> 01:19:05,980
- We used up all of our regular credits.
- Okay.

2048
01:19:05,980 --> 01:19:08,850
We have to check
how much the index goes up...

2049
01:19:08,980 --> 01:19:11,310
- based on the credits your teams use.
- Right.

2050
01:19:11,310 --> 01:19:12,580
- We have to check that.
- Yes.

2051
01:19:12,580 --> 01:19:14,320
- We only have regular credits.
- Yes.

2052
01:19:14,320 --> 01:19:17,090
It'd be nice to check the index tomorrow.

2053
01:19:19,920 --> 01:19:24,030
Next, there are two items on the agenda
that require your decisions.

2054
01:19:24,130 --> 01:19:25,860
- The first item on the agenda.
- Okay.

2055
01:19:25,860 --> 01:19:30,530
Providing a life
to open the supermarket the next day.

2056
01:19:30,530 --> 01:19:34,240
To pass this item,
the majority must stand in agreement.

2057
01:19:34,240 --> 01:19:38,840
The team providing the life must agree.

2058
01:19:38,840 --> 01:19:41,180
Any transfer of resources
executed without negotiation...

2059
01:19:41,180 --> 01:19:43,080
or outside the Trading Station...

2060
01:19:43,080 --> 01:19:45,080
will not be recognized by the system.

2061
01:19:45,080 --> 01:19:47,220
Please keep this in mind.

2062
01:19:47,220 --> 01:19:49,620
Discuss whether or not
you would provide a life...

2063
01:19:49,620 --> 01:19:52,460
to open Black's supermarket the next day.

2064
01:19:52,460 --> 01:19:53,790
Once the negotiation reaches an agreement,

2065
01:19:53,790 --> 01:19:56,730
say, "Negotiation complete."

2066
01:19:57,430 --> 01:19:59,560
- Let me explain this.
- Okay.

2067
01:19:59,560 --> 01:20:02,400
It's impossible for me to make any trades.

2068
01:20:02,570 --> 01:20:04,700
There's no possible way
for me to obtain a life.

2069
01:20:04,870 --> 01:20:07,570
I've tried all kinds of things.

2070
01:20:07,570 --> 01:20:10,640
Life acquisition outside the system...

2071
01:20:10,640 --> 01:20:12,380
won't be recognized.

2072
01:20:12,380 --> 01:20:15,580
It means I won't be able to use
the life I acquired today.

2073
01:20:16,250 --> 01:20:19,180
The announcement said
any resource acquisition...

2074
01:20:19,180 --> 01:20:21,990
executed outside the system
wouldn't be recognized.

2075
01:20:21,990 --> 01:20:24,420
Since I traded on the black market,
it was done outside the system.

2076
01:20:25,190 --> 01:20:27,460
"So this isn't mine."

2077
01:20:28,190 --> 01:20:29,290
So many thoughts
were going through my head.

2078
01:20:29,290 --> 01:20:31,860
"Should I return this? What do I do?"

2079
01:20:32,230 --> 01:20:33,930
Only during the Leader Negotiation,

2080
01:20:33,930 --> 01:20:36,570
you can provide me with one life.

2081
01:20:36,570 --> 01:20:40,400
And it's only possible with your agreement
since you hold the lives.

2082
01:20:40,500 --> 01:20:41,700
I think that sums it up.

2083
01:20:41,940 --> 01:20:45,480
I'd be really grateful
if you agree to give me one life.

2084
01:20:45,480 --> 01:20:49,480
I know that
each life is incredibly precious.

2085
01:20:49,480 --> 01:20:51,410
If you decide not to provide me with one,

2086
01:20:51,410 --> 01:20:53,350
I won't resent you for it.

2087
01:20:53,720 --> 01:20:56,550
However, if you don't give me a life,
the supermarket tomorrow...

2088
01:20:56,590 --> 01:20:59,020
- It won't open?
- It won't open at all.

2089
01:20:59,020 --> 01:21:00,360
- You can't open it.
- Actually,

2090
01:21:00,490 --> 01:21:03,230
it's a huge financial loss for me.

2091
01:21:03,230 --> 01:21:06,700
I'd like to remind you that
after another exhausting day,

2092
01:21:06,760 --> 01:21:08,570
everyone will get hungry...

2093
01:21:08,570 --> 01:21:12,100
and be on edge while playing games.

2094
01:21:12,340 --> 01:21:16,110
I think going without food for one day
might not be a bad idea.

2095
01:21:16,110 --> 01:21:17,410
If the majority agrees,

2096
01:21:17,410 --> 01:21:20,410
I don't have to make money for a day.

2097
01:21:22,010 --> 01:21:23,650
Given the circumstances,

2098
01:21:23,650 --> 01:21:25,480
I decided to pretend that
I was putting the community first.

2099
01:21:25,480 --> 01:21:27,680
"I'll sacrifice my profits."

2100
01:21:27,720 --> 01:21:29,890
"You should protect your lives."

2101
01:21:30,720 --> 01:21:32,760
I won't hold it against you...

2102
01:21:32,760 --> 01:21:34,820
if you disagree.

2103
01:21:35,560 --> 01:21:37,930
I have a question.

2104
01:21:37,930 --> 01:21:40,530
- On Day One,
- Yes?

2105
01:21:40,800 --> 01:21:42,870
they didn't give you any life?

2106
01:21:42,870 --> 01:21:44,900
- They only gave me one. Yes.
- Is that so?

2107
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:49,110
But you need to keep
running the supermarket.

2108
01:21:49,110 --> 01:21:52,880
I just assumed that you were already
given the lives you'd need...

2109
01:21:52,880 --> 01:21:55,910
to run the supermarket until the last day.

2110
01:21:56,010 --> 01:21:58,450
- I was flustered that I only had one.
- But if that's not the case...

2111
01:21:58,580 --> 01:22:01,020
On Day One, we were informed that...

2112
01:22:01,020 --> 01:22:02,820
there were 43 lives.

2113
01:22:02,820 --> 01:22:05,390
The distribution of the lives
isn't what we had in mind.

2114
01:22:06,120 --> 01:22:08,160
- If you don't have any lives with you,
- He's right.

2115
01:22:08,160 --> 01:22:09,730
the numbers don't add up.

2116
01:22:10,130 --> 01:22:13,260
One of the teams
is holding onto a lot of lives.

2117
01:22:13,860 --> 01:22:16,470
I'd like to point out that
I don't have any lives with me.

2118
01:22:16,470 --> 01:22:19,200
Once the supermarket
doesn't open tomorrow,

2119
01:22:19,200 --> 01:22:20,700
that should confirm it.

2120
01:22:20,700 --> 01:22:23,210
I don't see
how else I can prove this to you.

2121
01:22:23,210 --> 01:22:24,540
- Okay.
- Okay.

2122
01:22:28,480 --> 01:22:33,120
(At this rate,
everyone will have to starve.)

2123
01:22:36,590 --> 01:22:39,420
Actually, the only team
that can afford to give a life...

2124
01:22:39,420 --> 01:22:41,960
is Team Blue. But you guys...

2125
01:22:41,990 --> 01:22:43,690
are short on lives. Right?

2126
01:22:44,490 --> 01:22:47,660
So it's not easy to give away one life.

2127
01:22:48,100 --> 01:22:49,200
Right?

2128
01:22:49,700 --> 01:22:50,830
Yes.

2129
01:22:51,330 --> 01:22:52,770
Here's the thing.

2130
01:22:53,170 --> 01:22:55,770
With all due respect,

2131
01:22:56,010 --> 01:23:00,740
the current value of lives
is far too great.

2132
01:23:02,150 --> 01:23:03,750
To tell you the truth,

2133
01:23:04,110 --> 01:23:06,380
even our perspectives are not aligned.

2134
01:23:06,380 --> 01:23:09,090
- My team is divided too.
- Okay.

2135
01:23:09,620 --> 01:23:11,990
So before coming here,

2136
01:23:11,990 --> 01:23:13,960
I told them
I wouldn't commit to anything...

2137
01:23:13,960 --> 01:23:16,230
- we didn't agree on first.
- I see.

2138
01:23:17,330 --> 01:23:18,490
Well,

2139
01:23:18,490 --> 01:23:22,330
it looked like we were the only team
that could afford to provide a life.

2140
01:23:22,330 --> 01:23:24,530
If the supermarket closes,

2141
01:23:24,530 --> 01:23:27,270
no one will be able to eat any food.

2142
01:23:27,270 --> 01:23:29,710
Hunger drives people crazy.

2143
01:23:29,710 --> 01:23:33,510
Then I thought
there could be more incidents...

2144
01:23:33,510 --> 01:23:37,150
that might expose my team to danger.

2145
01:23:37,310 --> 01:23:40,080
"Should I just give him a life?"

2146
01:23:40,080 --> 01:23:42,720
"Should I just give him one..."

2147
01:23:42,720 --> 01:23:45,120
"and tell the girls to deduct one
from my share?"

2148
01:23:45,460 --> 01:23:46,620
"What do I do?"

2149
01:23:46,690 --> 01:23:49,730
I knew that both of them
would be dead set against this idea.

2150
01:23:49,930 --> 01:23:51,330
I could hear Genie's voice.

2151
01:23:51,330 --> 01:23:52,960
I could hear Pitou's voice too.

2152
01:23:53,030 --> 01:23:54,130
"Why would you do that?"

2153
01:23:54,130 --> 01:23:56,200
"We can just starve."

2154
01:23:56,200 --> 01:23:58,170
I can hear their voices,
talking like this.

2155
01:23:58,170 --> 01:24:00,170
(Salt, Writer)

2156
01:24:00,270 --> 01:24:01,740
It's too valuable.

2157
01:24:01,740 --> 01:24:02,910
I'm the leader.

2158
01:24:02,910 --> 01:24:06,340
But I made a promise to my team
before coming here.

2159
01:24:07,140 --> 01:24:08,680
I'm not sure...

2160
01:24:08,680 --> 01:24:12,250
if I can just make this decision
without running it by my team first.

2161
01:24:12,380 --> 01:24:13,920
- You're the leader.
- This is...

2162
01:24:13,920 --> 01:24:15,690
You don't need their permission.

2163
01:24:17,690 --> 01:24:18,820
It's...

2164
01:24:18,820 --> 01:24:20,990
If you insert only one of these later,

2165
01:24:20,990 --> 01:24:22,660
you won't need their permission. Right?

2166
01:24:24,330 --> 01:24:25,500
He's a scary one.

2167
01:24:25,500 --> 01:24:27,660
You must know that leaders have
this power over them.

2168
01:24:28,670 --> 01:24:30,230
At the end of each day,

2169
01:24:30,230 --> 01:24:31,500
if you insert a life...

2170
01:24:31,570 --> 01:24:33,970
only under your name, only you'll survive.

2171
01:24:33,970 --> 01:24:36,110
Then you won't need more lives.

2172
01:24:36,770 --> 01:24:38,740
So do you really need their permission?

2173
01:24:40,510 --> 01:24:41,940
I mean, you brought it up.

2174
01:24:45,880 --> 01:24:48,720
I understand that
you represent your team.

2175
01:24:48,720 --> 01:24:50,820
- But you're here...
- Right.

2176
01:24:50,820 --> 01:24:52,290
as their leader.

2177
01:24:52,290 --> 01:24:54,560
I do think as a leader,
you have to make these tough decisions...

2178
01:24:54,560 --> 01:24:56,730
and be able to use your power.

2179
01:24:56,730 --> 01:24:58,860
I understand your point very clearly.

2180
01:24:58,860 --> 01:25:01,130
- Wait. I'm not following.
- Yes.

2181
01:25:01,460 --> 01:25:03,070
Is it possible for the leader...

2182
01:25:03,070 --> 01:25:05,170
to stay on without holding any life?

2183
01:25:05,170 --> 01:25:06,940
No. If there's only one resident left
in the team,

2184
01:25:06,940 --> 01:25:08,070
you don't need any lives after that point.

2185
01:25:08,070 --> 01:25:09,610
- Right.
- Yes.

2186
01:25:09,670 --> 01:25:11,870
So it's when we insert the lives.

2187
01:25:11,870 --> 01:25:14,180
- I see. There's a way you can kill off...
- If you don't insert...

2188
01:25:14,180 --> 01:25:15,910
- the other residents?
- Right.

2189
01:25:15,910 --> 01:25:17,710
Every leader has that power.

2190
01:25:17,710 --> 01:25:19,950
It's just that no one has done it so far.

2191
01:25:21,420 --> 01:25:23,990
Currently,
this is the only power leaders have.

2192
01:25:24,090 --> 01:25:25,120
My heart is pounding.

2193
01:25:25,120 --> 01:25:26,190
So...

2194
01:25:26,190 --> 01:25:28,060
- let's say I insert only one life today.
- Yes.

2195
01:25:28,060 --> 01:25:29,090
Then...

2196
01:25:29,090 --> 01:25:30,190
- The other two will get eliminated.
- It doesn't...

2197
01:25:30,190 --> 01:25:31,330
It doesn't matter what remains?

2198
01:25:31,330 --> 01:25:32,560
- Right.
- They'll get eliminated?

2199
01:25:32,560 --> 01:25:33,760
- Right. They must leave.
- That's right.

2200
01:25:33,760 --> 01:25:35,730
- The submission finalizes it.
- Then...

2201
01:25:35,730 --> 01:25:38,070
the role of a leader
became so important starting today.

2202
01:25:38,070 --> 01:25:39,640
- Yes. It's always been important.
- It was important yesterday too.

2203
01:25:39,640 --> 01:25:42,240
- It was important yesterday too.
- No. This changes everything now.

2204
01:25:42,240 --> 01:25:44,010
- I see. She didn't tell you yesterday.
- Considering...

2205
01:25:44,010 --> 01:25:46,010
the personalities of my teammates,

2206
01:25:46,110 --> 01:25:48,280
there will be a lot of changes
based on who takes the position of leader.

2207
01:25:48,980 --> 01:25:50,810
You didn't know about this.

2208
01:25:51,410 --> 01:25:53,920
Genie didn't tell us...

2209
01:25:53,920 --> 01:25:57,020
that if I submitted my life only,

2210
01:25:57,020 --> 01:25:58,750
I could be the only one to survive.

2211
01:25:58,750 --> 01:26:01,820
I don't remember her telling us.

2212
01:26:02,020 --> 01:26:04,730
I never imagined
that could even be possible.

2213
01:26:04,960 --> 01:26:08,630
The biggest thing I've realized
about being a leader...

2214
01:26:08,630 --> 01:26:10,370
is that I could kill everyone
and survive on my own.

2215
01:26:10,500 --> 01:26:12,670
In such a situation,

2216
01:26:12,940 --> 01:26:15,300
Genie could easily kill me...

2217
01:26:15,300 --> 01:26:16,470
if she wanted to.

2218
01:26:17,210 --> 01:26:20,210
So if there's someone you think...

2219
01:26:20,210 --> 01:26:24,610
could be a threat...

2220
01:26:24,780 --> 01:26:27,120
to you being re-elected tomorrow,

2221
01:26:27,120 --> 01:26:30,020
you'd need to talk...

2222
01:26:30,420 --> 01:26:31,920
to the other person in advance...

2223
01:26:31,920 --> 01:26:33,160
for the sake of your survival.

2224
01:26:34,320 --> 01:26:36,330
We all know...

2225
01:26:36,330 --> 01:26:38,230
that the lives are running out.

2226
01:26:38,230 --> 01:26:40,230
This place is really scary.

2227
01:26:40,460 --> 01:26:42,030
- It's really scary.
- You have to think carefully.

2228
01:26:42,030 --> 01:26:43,970
The leaders...

2229
01:26:43,970 --> 01:26:45,430
can kill their own members.

2230
01:26:45,430 --> 01:26:46,540
- Of course.
- That's right.

2231
01:26:48,170 --> 01:26:49,240
Of course.

2232
01:26:50,270 --> 01:26:52,540
Being the leader is quite scary.

2233
01:26:52,710 --> 01:26:54,180
But we won't do that.

2234
01:26:55,080 --> 01:26:56,910
There are people who can do it.

2235
01:26:57,450 --> 01:26:59,820
That's right.
We'll see such people soon or later.

2236
01:26:59,820 --> 01:27:01,080
They'll try to become the leader.

2237
01:27:03,790 --> 01:27:06,890
I hope Team Blue's leader
doesn't get changed to Genie.

2238
01:27:07,320 --> 01:27:09,530
I can persuade Salt.

2239
01:27:09,660 --> 01:27:14,560
She doesn't seem to have much will
to exploit the authority.

2240
01:27:15,000 --> 01:27:18,670
That's why I kept saying
I wanted Salt to be the leader.

2241
01:27:19,670 --> 01:27:21,740
I thought someone in Team Blue
will soon get to die.

2242
01:27:22,270 --> 01:27:24,610
It looked like the members weren't
on the same page yet.

2243
01:27:24,710 --> 01:27:27,580
I hope Salt survives the longest.

2244
01:27:27,580 --> 01:27:29,780
She's the easiest to trade with.

2245
01:27:30,980 --> 01:27:32,080
(Exclaiming)

2246
01:27:32,080 --> 01:27:33,150
Should I kill her?

2247
01:27:33,280 --> 01:27:35,080
Would she try to kill me if I kill her?

2248
01:27:36,050 --> 01:27:37,120
What should I do?

2249
01:27:37,320 --> 01:27:39,460
I'm most scared of Genie.

2250
01:27:39,720 --> 01:27:41,860
Our opinions are different.

2251
01:27:42,020 --> 01:27:43,930
It's so clear...

2252
01:27:44,230 --> 01:27:46,560
that she puts herself first.

2253
01:27:46,560 --> 01:27:47,760
She's a transparent person.

2254
01:27:47,760 --> 01:27:49,770
Since she's so transparent,

2255
01:27:49,770 --> 01:27:51,770
I can tell that
I could always be in danger...

2256
01:27:51,770 --> 01:27:54,170
if she goes by her standard.

2257
01:27:54,170 --> 01:27:56,540
She's like an early warning.

2258
01:27:59,480 --> 01:28:02,110
- Shall we move on to the second item?
- Yes.

2259
01:28:02,510 --> 01:28:04,910
It looks like we've settled the agenda.

2260
01:28:04,910 --> 01:28:07,980
It seems like Team Blue
won't be providing any lives today.

2261
01:28:08,950 --> 01:28:10,490
You won't be running
the supermarket tomorrow.

2262
01:28:10,490 --> 01:28:12,290
That's right. I'm jobless.

2263
01:28:12,490 --> 01:28:14,320
The negotiations have failed.

2264
01:28:14,320 --> 01:28:16,560
The supermarket will close down tomorrow.

2265
01:28:16,560 --> 01:28:18,630
Moving on to the next item on the agenda.

2266
01:28:20,930 --> 01:28:23,900
I should have stored a lot earlier.

2267
01:28:28,040 --> 01:28:29,040
Tomorrow,

2268
01:28:29,940 --> 01:28:32,340
we should have eggs and bananas...

2269
01:28:32,340 --> 01:28:33,540
- That's right.
- for breakfast.

2270
01:28:35,180 --> 01:28:36,450
(Exclaiming)

2271
01:28:36,450 --> 01:28:37,580
Our impoverished...

2272
01:28:37,710 --> 01:28:38,810
We're poor.

2273
01:28:39,550 --> 01:28:41,380
We can spend some.

2274
01:28:41,380 --> 01:28:43,390
- Let's eat well tomorrow.
- Okay.

2275
01:28:44,150 --> 01:28:45,720
The second item on the agenda.

2276
01:28:45,920 --> 01:28:49,460
This concerns the decision
to provide aid or impose sanctions.

2277
01:28:49,460 --> 01:28:51,160
First is aid.

2278
01:28:51,160 --> 01:28:53,130
If a majority of the leaders agree,

2279
01:28:53,130 --> 01:28:56,570
resources currently in their possession...

2280
01:28:56,570 --> 01:28:58,470
may be transferred between two teams...

2281
01:28:58,470 --> 01:29:01,500
without spending any credits.

2282
01:29:01,770 --> 01:29:03,570
Next is sanctions.

2283
01:29:03,710 --> 01:29:05,640
If a majority of the leaders agree,

2284
01:29:05,640 --> 01:29:09,810
one team will be prohibited from using
the Trading Station for the following day.

2285
01:29:10,310 --> 01:29:12,210
Only one of the two options,

2286
01:29:12,210 --> 01:29:15,280
aid or sanctions, can be implemented.

2287
01:29:15,280 --> 01:29:17,420
If no agreement is reached,

2288
01:29:17,420 --> 01:29:19,190
the negotiation period will end.

2289
01:29:19,190 --> 01:29:20,990
- Sanctions.
- Once the negotiation is complete,

2290
01:29:20,990 --> 01:29:23,660
please say, "Negotiation complete."

2291
01:29:24,090 --> 01:29:26,030
That's stopping a team
from making any trades, right?

2292
01:29:26,800 --> 01:29:28,300
There's no benefit to the community.

2293
01:29:28,560 --> 01:29:29,730
So far, that's right.

2294
01:29:29,770 --> 01:29:31,330
Is it a must to choose one of the options?

2295
01:29:31,330 --> 01:29:32,340
No, we can decide to choose none.

2296
01:29:32,340 --> 01:29:34,240
- We can decide to choose none.
- Right?

2297
01:29:34,640 --> 01:29:36,540
And if we are to choose,
we can only choose one of them.

2298
01:29:36,540 --> 01:29:38,710
We can only choose one of those options.

2299
01:29:38,710 --> 01:29:42,110
Will this item come up every day?

2300
01:29:42,280 --> 01:29:45,250
I think so.
I think the second item came up...

2301
01:29:45,250 --> 01:29:48,220
to tell us that we could provide aid...

2302
01:29:48,650 --> 01:29:50,650
or impose sanctions.

2303
01:29:51,150 --> 01:29:54,020
It's hard to make a decision today...

2304
01:29:54,020 --> 01:29:56,390
since we didn't know anything about this.

2305
01:29:56,630 --> 01:29:58,960
- That's true.
- No team needs aid now, right?

2306
01:29:59,260 --> 01:30:01,560
We don't really need aid right now,

2307
01:30:01,560 --> 01:30:03,630
- but I'm sure the need will come up.
- Tomorrow...

2308
01:30:03,770 --> 01:30:06,300
Also, about what I mentioned earlier,

2309
01:30:06,300 --> 01:30:08,200
- in your rooms...
- That's right.

2310
01:30:08,200 --> 01:30:09,410
There's a code
on the wall with the TV, right?

2311
01:30:09,410 --> 01:30:10,540
- Yes.
- We have one.

2312
01:30:10,540 --> 01:30:12,840
I'm really curious to know what's there.

2313
01:30:12,840 --> 01:30:14,880
If there are lives there,

2314
01:30:14,880 --> 01:30:16,310
I think we should break it.

2315
01:30:16,780 --> 01:30:18,910
I don't think we can get lives...

2316
01:30:18,910 --> 01:30:21,550
only through productive activities.

2317
01:30:21,550 --> 01:30:23,350
- That's right.
- In that case,

2318
01:30:24,020 --> 01:30:26,490
even if Teams White, Red, and Blue...

2319
01:30:26,490 --> 01:30:28,760
answer all the questions right,

2320
01:30:28,760 --> 01:30:31,530
we can't coexist...

2321
01:30:31,530 --> 01:30:32,830
- with this number.
- That's right.

2322
01:30:33,500 --> 01:30:35,360
Let's talk about this outside.

2323
01:30:35,360 --> 01:30:38,570
I think we should quickly
solve the codes in our room...

2324
01:30:38,570 --> 01:30:41,070
and make those resources communal.

2325
01:30:41,070 --> 01:30:43,570
Are you sure
they're resources in the first place?

2326
01:30:43,570 --> 01:30:46,240
We don't know. But to just do nothing,

2327
01:30:46,240 --> 01:30:49,950
the pressure is closing in on us quickly.

2328
01:30:49,950 --> 01:30:51,950
So I want us to find more resources.

2329
01:30:51,950 --> 01:30:54,980
The resources we're mining...

2330
01:30:54,980 --> 01:30:56,350
aren't enough.

2331
01:30:56,350 --> 01:30:58,490
- We already solved it.
- Really?

2332
01:30:58,490 --> 01:31:00,320
We solved it the day we got here.

2333
01:31:00,320 --> 01:31:02,120
We solved it in 30 minutes
the day we got here.

2334
01:31:02,120 --> 01:31:04,790
We're wondering if all the other rooms...

2335
01:31:04,790 --> 01:31:05,900
have the same code.

2336
01:31:06,160 --> 01:31:08,230
Is it a code
that has to be brought together,

2337
01:31:08,230 --> 01:31:10,700
or does everyone have the same code?
That's our question.

2338
01:31:10,700 --> 01:31:14,240
If it's the same code,
we'll try to find more resources...

2339
01:31:14,240 --> 01:31:16,640
with the solution we got.

2340
01:31:16,770 --> 01:31:20,010
If not, I'm saying this
to change the way...

2341
01:31:20,010 --> 01:31:21,040
of finding resources.

2342
01:31:21,040 --> 01:31:24,310
I'm curious about your codes.

2343
01:31:24,310 --> 01:31:26,350
If any team is willing
to share it with us,

2344
01:31:26,350 --> 01:31:27,880
we'll try to share the resources...

2345
01:31:27,880 --> 01:31:29,790
we get out of it...

2346
01:31:29,790 --> 01:31:31,990
with that team.

2347
01:31:31,990 --> 01:31:33,420
We'll try to make that happen.

2348
01:31:33,560 --> 01:31:35,320
If it's the code you're talking about,

2349
01:31:35,520 --> 01:31:38,830
I think I can share it with you
using my authority as the leader.

2350
01:31:38,830 --> 01:31:39,900
Then we can do that after this ends.

2351
01:31:39,900 --> 01:31:41,030
- We can do it outside...
- Yes.

2352
01:31:41,030 --> 01:31:43,200
- if that's possible.
- I'll share it with you.

2353
01:31:43,430 --> 01:31:44,430
All right.

2354
01:31:44,930 --> 01:31:46,370
I'm doomed.

2355
01:31:46,870 --> 01:31:49,810
If there are three leaders,
they'll most likely agree.

2356
01:31:49,810 --> 01:31:52,040
How can I say no to that?

2357
01:31:52,040 --> 01:31:54,680
I'll be discovered right away
if they worked together.

2358
01:31:54,840 --> 01:31:56,750
I tried to keep a straight face...

2359
01:31:57,850 --> 01:32:00,550
and thought, "I should try
to win them over after the meeting."

2360
01:32:00,880 --> 01:32:02,280
This is the biggest crisis of my life.

2361
01:32:03,450 --> 01:32:05,190
Then...

2362
01:32:05,190 --> 01:32:07,560
- Negotiation failed.
- Negotiation failed.

2363
01:32:09,630 --> 01:32:10,690
It's so scary.

2364
01:32:10,790 --> 01:32:13,130
- All negotiations are complete.
- Okay.

2365
01:32:13,130 --> 01:32:16,200
We'll move on to today's life submission.

2366
01:32:17,630 --> 01:32:19,070
Who's going to start?

2367
01:32:19,070 --> 01:32:21,100
- I'll go last.
- I'll go first.

2368
01:32:21,100 --> 01:32:22,200
Sure. Go ahead.

2369
01:32:22,400 --> 01:32:23,710
It's so scary.

2370
01:32:23,710 --> 01:32:24,840
I've got chills.

2371
01:32:24,840 --> 01:32:26,480
I don't know what to do.

2372
01:32:27,140 --> 01:32:30,510
You have to protect your power.

2373
01:32:32,250 --> 01:32:34,580
Think about it. You won't...

2374
01:32:34,950 --> 01:32:37,550
submit 2 lives when you have 3.

2375
01:32:37,950 --> 01:32:40,860
You shouldn't let someone
who could do that become the leader.

2376
01:32:41,360 --> 01:32:44,430
I didn't think about that...

2377
01:32:44,830 --> 01:32:47,060
when Pitou was the leader.

2378
01:32:47,800 --> 01:32:48,800
But...

2379
01:32:49,270 --> 01:32:51,430
You think it'll be a bit risky
when Genie becomes the leader?

2380
01:32:52,100 --> 01:32:53,840
I think there's a possibility.

2381
01:32:57,710 --> 01:33:00,410
(Dormitory for Blue)

2382
01:33:00,640 --> 01:33:02,280
- Genie.
- Yes?

2383
01:33:02,780 --> 01:33:04,210
Do you think...

2384
01:33:04,580 --> 01:33:05,950
we can survive?

2385
01:33:07,520 --> 01:33:09,220
You're suddenly worried about that?

2386
01:33:09,290 --> 01:33:12,760
Suddenly...
I really like this peaceful state.

2387
01:33:14,690 --> 01:33:16,530
I want to do better since we're a team.

2388
01:33:17,030 --> 01:33:18,090
Right.

2389
01:33:18,260 --> 01:33:21,100
You feel more responsible.

2390
01:33:21,100 --> 01:33:23,670
It certainly feels different...

2391
01:33:23,670 --> 01:33:24,970
compared to when I played it by myself.

2392
01:33:25,570 --> 01:33:28,070
But you still have plenty of lives.

2393
01:33:28,070 --> 01:33:29,170
So far, yes.

2394
01:33:29,170 --> 01:33:31,110
You might get your turn again.

2395
01:33:31,840 --> 01:33:34,240
But everyone's standard
of "plenty" is different.

2396
01:33:34,240 --> 01:33:35,910
Of course.

2397
01:33:36,550 --> 01:33:39,420
Your life submission is complete.

2398
01:33:39,420 --> 01:33:41,450
You may now leave.

2399
01:33:41,450 --> 01:33:44,490
(Everyone in Team Red survives Day 2.)

2400
01:33:44,490 --> 01:33:46,560
You can get re-elected through voting.

2401
01:33:46,560 --> 01:33:47,560
That's right.

2402
01:33:47,620 --> 01:33:49,490
That way, you can keep your power.

2403
01:33:49,930 --> 01:33:51,160
I'm done.

2404
01:33:51,530 --> 01:33:54,200
- Well done.
- I think I could do it through voting.

2405
01:33:54,530 --> 01:33:55,830
- For now...
- Go ahead.

2406
01:33:55,830 --> 01:33:58,070
After Pitou,
it was to be decided through voting.

2407
01:33:58,500 --> 01:33:59,600
- What is it?
- They decided to take turns...

2408
01:33:59,600 --> 01:34:01,400
- being the leader.
- I see.

2409
01:34:02,640 --> 01:34:04,770
Please check the contents
of the central box...

2410
01:34:04,970 --> 01:34:09,110
and assign lives
to the residents of your choice.

2411
01:34:09,180 --> 01:34:10,180
Okay.

2412
01:34:25,860 --> 01:34:30,770
(Life Submission for Day 2)

2413
01:34:41,910 --> 01:34:43,250
I'm so nervous.

2414
01:34:59,260 --> 01:35:02,870
(Life Submission for Day 2)

2415
01:35:09,510 --> 01:35:11,370
(Life Submission for Day 2)

2416
01:35:21,380 --> 01:35:22,580
(Salt, Pitou)

2417
01:35:25,390 --> 01:35:29,760
(Salt, Genie, Pitou)

2418
01:35:46,110 --> 01:35:47,340
Today's my chance.

2419
01:35:47,710 --> 01:35:52,950
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
